<node id="4ac4d845-23a9-4953-a088-29b4a743018c">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Term Life Insurance Overview","text":"instatement Period: 5 Years from Lapse  \nPremiums are level and guaranteed not to increase during the guaranteed term period. \nCoverage will terminate at the end of the term unless renewed or converted as specified in \nthe contract. All benefits are subject to the terms and exclusions outlined in the policy.\n\n===== Page 3 =====\nDEFINITIONS  \nPolicy: This Individual Term Life Insurance contract, including the application, policy \nschedule, riders, and endorsements.  \nCompany: Sentinel Life Assurance Company.  \nInsured: The person whose life is covered under this policy.  \nOwner: The person who has all rights of ownership under the policy.  \nBeneficiary: The person(s) designated to receive the Death Benefit upon the Insured’s death.  \nDeath Benefit: The amount payable to the Beneficiary upon the Insured’s death, subject to \nthe terms of this policy.  \nPremium: The payment required to keep the policy in force.  \nGrace Period: A 31-day period following a missed premium during which the policy remains \nin force. Reinstatement: The process by which a lapsed policy may be restored to active \nstatus.  \nIncontestability Period: A two-year period during which the Company may contest the \nvalidity of the policy based on material misrepresentations.\n\n===== Page 4 =====\nPOLICY PROVISIONS – PART I  \nEntire Contract  \nThis policy, together with the application and any attached riders or endorsements, constitutes \nthe entire contract between the Policy Owner and the Company. No agent or representative \nmay alter or waive any provision of this policy unless expressly authorized in writing by an \nofficer of the Company.  \nConsideration  \nThis policy is issued in consideration of the statements made in the application and the \npayment of the first premium. Continued coverage is subject to the timely payment of all \nsubsequent premiums due.  \nEffective Date  \nThe Effective Date of this policy is shown on the Schedule of Benefits. Coverage begins at \n12:01 A.M. Standard Time at the Owner’s address on that date.  \nOwnership  \nThe Policy Owner possesses all contractual rights, including the right to change \nbeneficiaries, assign the policy, and request cancellation. If no Owner is named, the \nInsured shall be deemed the Owner.  \nRight to Examine Policy  \nThe Owner has the right to examine this policy for a period of 20 days from receipt. If not \nsatisfied,","summary":"This document details an individual term life insurance policy with a 5-year guaranteed term where premiums are fixed and non-increasing. Key terms such as Insured, Owner, Beneficiary, and Death Benefit are defined, along with important policy mechanisms like grace periods, reinstatement, and incontestability. Core provisions include the policy being the entire contract, effective dates tied to issuance, full ownership rights vested in the owner, and a 20-day examination period for the policyholder.","topics":["Term Life Insurance","Policy Provisions","Insurance Definitions","Contractual Terms"],"facts":[{"name":"Reinstatement Window Duration","sentence":"The instatement period is 5 years from lapse.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["reinstatement period","policy lapse","coverage restoration"],"entities":[{"name":"Sentinel Life Assurance Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer of the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person whose life is covered","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"contractual holder of policy rights","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"amount paid after insured's death","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Premium","type":"CONCEPT","role":"periodic payment to maintain coverage","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Grace Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"31-day window post-missed payment","relational_anchors":["31-day"]},{"name":"Reinstatement","type":"CONCEPT","role":"restoration of lapsed policy status","relational_anchors":["from Lapse"]},{"name":"Incontestability Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"two-year challenge window for validity","relational_anchors":["two-year"]},{"name":"Entire Contract","type":"CONCEPT","role":"complete binding agreement definition","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Consideration","type":"CONCEPT","role":"basis for issuing the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Effective Date","type":"CONCEPT","role":"start point of coverage activation","relational_anchors":["Schedule of Benefits"]},{"name":"Right to Examine Policy","type":"CONCEPT","role":"20-day review period for owner","relational_anchors":["20 days"]}]},{"name":"Level Premium Guarantee","sentence":"Premiums are level during the guaranteed term period.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["premium guarantee","guaranteed term period","policy cost stability"],"entities":[{"name":"Sentinel Life Assurance Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer of the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person whose life is covered","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"contractual holder of policy rights","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"amount paid after insured's death","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Premium","type":"CONCEPT","role":"periodic payment to maintain coverage","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Grace Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"31-day window post-missed payment","relational_anchors":["31-day"]},{"name":"Reinstatement","type":"CONCEPT","role":"restoration of lapsed policy status","relational_anchors":["from Lapse"]},{"name":"Incontestability Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"two-year challenge window for validity","relational_anchors":["two-year"]},{"name":"Entire Contract","type":"CONCEPT","role":"complete binding agreement definition","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Consideration","type":"CONCEPT","role":"basis for issuing the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Effective Date","type":"CONCEPT","role":"start point of coverage activation","relational_anchors":["Schedule of Benefits"]},{"name":"Right to Examine Policy","type":"CONCEPT","role":"20-day review period for owner","relational_anchors":["20 days"]}]},{"name":"Guaranteed Level Premiums","sentence":"Premiums are guaranteed not to increase during the guaranteed term period.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["guaranteed term period","level premiums","premium guarantees"],"entities":[{"name":"Sentinel Life Assurance Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer of the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person whose life is covered","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"contractual holder of policy rights","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"amount paid after insured's death","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Premium","type":"CONCEPT","role":"periodic payment to maintain coverage","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Grace Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"31-day window post-missed payment","relational_anchors":["31-day"]},{"name":"Reinstatement","type":"CONCEPT","role":"restoration of lapsed policy status","relational_anchors":["from Lapse"]},{"name":"Incontestability Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"two-year challenge window for validity","relational_anchors":["two-year"]},{"name":"Entire Contract","type":"CONCEPT","role":"complete binding agreement definition","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Consideration","type":"CONCEPT","role":"basis for issuing the policy","relational_anchor