  <data key="d3">The rule that only written and signed changes from Sentinel Life Assurance Company’s officers are valid presupposes that the company is the legitimate entity governing the policy, reinforcing its role as the issuing insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">authorizes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="80518b2d-1bb2-4fa2-93b9-79573d720a98">
  <data key="d3">Any alteration to the policy requires written consent from Sentinel Life Assurance Company’s officers, regardless of who holds ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="3babd2b0-2bbd-47de-9b19-fa8ac968a0d5">
  <data key="d3">A requirement that all contract modifications be in writing and signed by a company officer ensures that changes to policies such as the specified 20-year level term life insurance are formally documented and legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="a8f33721-10d3-4a55-bd6d-b3fe229773e9">
  <data key="d3">Any modification to the contract must be in writing and signed by a company officer, ensuring compliance with the legal standards established by Colorado law.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="1967adef-ed54-4a4b-82ca-b7fa88d7aeb7">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written and signed amendments ensures enforceability and integrity of the legal contract established in fact_sentence_1, maintaining consistency with standard contractual practices.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="8553795c-a210-458d-bbd9-47de9966423a">
  <data key="d3">Any alteration to the contract’s obligations—including those related to paying the death benefit—is subject to formal documentation and executive approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="3c328b68-a332-4773-9c29-f646235f7d51">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 ensures that the terms governing the death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 cannot be changed without proper documentation, thereby preserving the original intent and scope of the coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="4c454305-8df7-4f9a-b113-fd49d2e08142">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written approval by a company officer ensures that only authorized changes to the contract—defined in the first sentence—are legally binding, reinforcing the boundaries of contractual modification.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="0d5e54d4-82aa-4712-9f7e-bdb99dc0e6ca">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written approval of contract changes ensures that provisions like the suicide exclusion cannot be altered informally. This maintains the integrity of such clauses once included in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="835b03af-5fa4-431f-80f1-d702c4462036">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the legal procedure for modifying the contract, ensuring only authorized changes take effect. This procedural rule applies directly to the policy described in fact_sentence_2, including its classification as a 20-Year Level Term plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets forth the legal procedure required for altering any terms of the policy, including premium guarantees. Fact_sentence_2 defines the specific length of time during which premiums remain guaranteed under the current contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider represents a contractual amendment requiring documentation and authorization per the insurer’s rules. This fact depends on the validity of written approval from a company officer as stipulated in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires documentation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="af0642b0-b73b-4d5a-941d-8b8a65fef5d4">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring written approval from a company officer ensures that any modification to the policy’s conditions—including those affecting premium structures—is formally documented. This reinforces the reliability of stated terms like fixed premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written approval from a company officer ensures that modifications to the policy's terms—including those affecting premiums—are formally documented. This supports the assurance that premiums remain unchanged throughout the term, as stated in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="5b53632e-6b25-4a1a-a6e8-a0b75be0df3a">
  <data key="d3">Any modification to the policy requires official written consent, ensuring that only authorized changes alter the contract; thus, all benefits paid must still conform strictly to the original or formally amended terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions benefits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">Change-of-beneficiary requests require written authorization from Sentinel Life’s officers to be valid, aligning with the rule that such changes become effective only after being properly executed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">A change of beneficiary requires a written, signed request approved by an officer of Sentinel Life Assurance Company to be legally valid, even though it takes effect on the date of signing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets a legal standard requiring written approval for contract amendments, which applies to beneficiary changes described in fact_sentence_2. This ensures that even though beneficiary updates take effect upon receipt, they remain legally binding only if compliant with the formal process outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the legal standard requiring written approval for changes, which applies to beneficiary amendments described in fact_sentence_2. This ensures that even though beneficiary changes take effect upon receipt, they remain legally binding only if compliant with the formal process outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="de0d67af-5b66-4374-8edd-cc82b199731b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written, officer-signed amendments to the policy is directly tied to individuals like Eleanor B. Raynor, whose position as CEO grants them authority to fulfill this condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec" target="57fafae6-d83d-473d-a0a2-e4e4d1824c40">
  <data key="d3">The clause requiring written approval from an officer supports the legitimacy of Eleanor B. Raynor’s ability to act on behalf of Sentinel Life Assurance Company in matters affecting contracts.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
