  <data key="d3">The presence of an accelerated death benefit rider indicates that the underlying policy supports optional add-ons; specifically, it confirms that the base policy is a 20-year level term life insurance product capable of being extended through such riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="dbe6ae57-ebfd-495c-82e2-7e10d5207bf3">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of the accelerated death benefit rider adds value to the policy, which is supported by the consistent monthly premium payment of $42.00.</data>
  <data key="d4">funding</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">The attachment of an accelerated death benefit rider enhances the policy's utility during critical health events, complementing the long-term stability offered by the 20-year guaranteed premium period.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="b90bc020-0e6f-4387-b39e-6c2e84c74262">
  <data key="d3">The presence of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider requires the policy to have started coverage, meaning its functionality hinges on the effective date of August 7, 2025.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
