  <data key="d3">The presence of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider enables early payouts for terminal illnesses, but fact_sentence_2 restricts eligibility when the illness results from self-inflicted harm, thereby limiting the scope of coverage despite the rider's existence.</data>
