  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period specifies when a lapsed policy may be revived, but its applicability depends entirely on the broader terms outlined in the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">subsumed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window complements the option to pay premiums monthly, enabling policyholders like Jordan to restore coverage after missing payments without losing benefits entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance explains the cause of potential lapses, making the 5-year reinstatement window relevant and actionable when payments fall behind.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 provides a specific instance of a 5-year reinstatement window tied to a policy’s lapse, while fact_sentence_2 generalizes this rule across policies, reinforcing the validity and applicability of the timeframe mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window depends on satisfying the requirement of providing evidence of insurability, which ensures the applicant remains eligible despite the lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement period allows for recovery after lapse, but only if outstanding premiums with interest are fully paid, which is explicitly stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement period preserves the possibility of maintaining active coverage, thereby enabling the death benefit to be paid to the beneficiary when the insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window enables the policyholder to restore coverage after lapse, ensuring continuity necessary for the insurer to fulfill its obligation to pay the death benefit upon verified death during active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses but is reinstated within the 5-year window, it may remain eligible for a lump-sum death benefit payment upon the insured’s passing, ensuring continuity of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement window allows recovery of a lapsed policy within five years, while acceptance of a certified death certificate ensures proper validation of a claim upon death; these processes operate at different stages of the policy timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
