<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="1bc20fef-0219-4067-93b4-960a572af52c">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums across the term implies consistency in coverage terms, which can be referenced using the assigned policy number.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="4de07664-40a5-4e8c-9078-ba2e3d911267">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of unchanging premiums implies institutional stability and credibility, reinforcing the significance of Sentinel Life Assurance Company as the reliable issuer of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="80518b2d-1bb2-4fa2-93b9-79573d720a98">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases implies stable financial obligations tied to the policy, consistent with the role of the named policyholder, Jordan Everett Hughes.</data>
  <data key="d4">ensures stability for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="8fc90088-9d80-42d0-8aba-0a66fc2bce8b">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums over the term implies that the financial obligations begin from the policy’s effective date, August 7, 2025.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="3babd2b0-2bbd-47de-9b19-fa8ac968a0d5">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won’t increase during the term reflects the defining characteristic of a level term life insurance policy, confirming that the policy maintains consistent pricing across its entire 20-year duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="1967adef-ed54-4a4b-82ca-b7fa88d7aeb7">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed stable premiums rely on the existence of a formal legal contract between the insurer and the policyholder, making this feature contingent upon the contractual basis established earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="8553795c-a210-458d-bbd9-47de9966423a">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed stable premiums make it possible for the company to honor its binding promise to disburse the death benefit to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="4c454305-8df7-4f9a-b113-fd49d2e08142">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed premium stability relies on being explicitly included within the formal contract documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforced by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed stable premiums mean that the insurer cannot raise payments without altering the contract, which requires a written, authorized change per the first statement, thus linking price stability to formal procedural safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="44a69e56-850d-4ea1-95b8-2226d8cfc678">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed premiums ensure consistent payments across the term, which aligns with the purpose of the contestability period—a defined window where underwriting accuracy is verified without sudden changes in coverage cost affecting beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="0d5e54d4-82aa-4712-9f7e-bdb99dc0e6ca">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed premiums provide stable cost predictability, whereas the suicide exclusion protects the insurer against certain high-risk scenarios; together they define core policy protections and limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="3fabbb3c-c938-4f7a-ab4d-20e58b9e5b05">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of unchanging premiums applies exclusively to the policyholder, Jordan Everett Hughes, confirming his central role in defining the policy's financial stability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="835b03af-5fa4-431f-80f1-d702c4462036">
  <data key="d3">The assurance that premiums will not rise during the term supports the characterization of the policy as a level term life insurance product, where consistent payments are maintained throughout the coverage period.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="c446b9c8-2ed6-4125-bd61-520aaa02f788">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums throughout the term reflects actuarial calculations based on the insured’s initial age of 37 at issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual support</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="f977fc63-d49f-485a-b170-30398a30ab1f">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed premiums mean the cost will not rise during the term, even if the insured’s risk profile were to change; however, the current standard non-smoker rating reflects the original underwriting decision.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="c60b044e-6ee5-4b98-90f3-c0a74783eec9">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed stable premiums mean the insured knows exactly what they’ll pay each month, making it easier to assess whether the $500,000 coverage provides sufficient value given consistent out-of-pocket expense.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="dbe6ae57-ebfd-495c-82e2-7e10d5207bf3">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won’t rise implies that the initially stated $42.00 monthly payment will remain unchanged throughout the entire term.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="ad1cb066-961b-4cae-bf88-48a316e04583">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed constant premiums make it feasible to set up automated monthly bank drafts without risk of fluctuating charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that premiums are locked in over the guaranteed term, providing concrete meaning to the 20-year premium guarantee mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="b90bc020-0e6f-4387-b39e-6c2e84c74262">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed premiums mean that payments will not rise over time, making them applicable from the moment coverage begins—specifically on August 7, 2025—as confirmed by the start date of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="d3b72487-817b-4bd9-9c48-3e22d25ec16e">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed constant premiums apply only over the term that ends on August 7, 2045.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="af0642b0-b73b-4d5a-941d-8b8a65fef5d4">
  <data key="d3">The assurance that premiums won’t increase (fact_sentence_2) implies they remain at a fixed rate, aligning with the concept of "level" premiums described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">equivalent to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="172b9278-1d92-4151-bb1c-57052cd17f3d">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed stability of premiums over the term implies financial predictability tied directly to the policy’s lifespan, which concludes at the end of the term if not extended.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="5b53632e-6b25-4a1a-a6e8-a0b75be0df3a">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums during the term is upheld only if all conditions specified in the contract are met, including compliance with clauses like the contestability period and suicide exclusion.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums over the term supports the predictability of the Death Benefit payment, ensuring the policy remains active and financially viable when needed.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 confirms premium stability over the term, reinforcing the reliability of coverage described in chunk_summary_1; fact_sentence_2 clarifies who receives benefits, providing essential meaning to the beneficiary designations already stated.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures financial predictability throughout the term, while the 20-day examination period allows the insured to cancel the policy without penalty early on. These clauses serve complementary roles in protecting the policyholder’s interests at different stages.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
