  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="e7816414-6dc8-4d4c-8612-6e33f02b37d5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="16a529f5-ae10-482a-9029-57548ed48ff5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="e6cf6fd4-1010-407f-851c-19423d8642ca">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="7d1e8f4b-0d2d-430c-8411-66f3d992551b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms that premiums cannot rise during the term, which logically implies they remain unchanged—thus aligning with and validating the claim made in fact_sentence_1 about levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums throughout the term provides financial certainty, which complements the understanding that coverage expires after five years if not extended.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums ensures predictable costs during the term, which aligns with the policy's finite duration described here. Coverage ceases after the term unless conversion occurs, making the fixed premium relevant only until termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums ensures predictable costs throughout the term, enabling the policyholder to plan financially when considering renewal or conversion options later.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about stable premiums applies specifically to the type of contract referred to as a "Policy," reinforcing its stability features within the defined scope.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of unchanging premiums ensures predictable payment obligations, allowing the insured to maintain coverage without fear of rising costs. However, even with stable premiums, any death benefit payout remains contingent upon compliance with the policy’s stated conditions and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable cost over time, which supports consistent access to coverage. This stability indirectly enables the Death Benefit to be paid according to the agreed-upon terms without disruption from rising costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">independently supports</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won’t increase relies on the definition of a premium as the necessary payment to sustain coverage. Without understanding what a premium is, the significance of it being fixed cannot be fully grasped.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums ensures predictable costs over time, allowing the policyholder to rely on consistent funding. This consistency enables the grace period mechanism to function effectively, maintaining coverage despite temporary delays in payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases relies on the policy's immutability; without authorized alterations, the fixed rate remains intact.</data>
  <data key="d4">ensures</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums relies on the policyholder fulfilling the obligation to pay the first premium, which triggers the start of the guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums ensures that policyholders can reliably meet their payment obligations, enabling continuous coverage if payments are made promptly.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">Fixed premiums ensure stable financial obligations, allowing the Policy Owner to reliably exercise full control over the policy without unexpected cost changes disrupting their rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable costs over time, allowing the policyholder confidence in ongoing affordability. This financial certainty supports the policyholder’s ability to exercise the right to cancel without unexpected cost burdens.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase ensures predictable costs over time, complementing the 20-day examination period, which allows the policyholder to review and potentially void the agreement if unsatisfied.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium guarantee ensures stability during the term, but if coverage lapses, reinstatement hinges on proving insurability—a factor that may undermine the original guarantee’s benefits if the insured becomes uninsurable later.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">A fixed premium guarantee ensures ongoing policy coverage, directly supporting the insurer’s ability to fulfill its commitment to pay the death benefit when the insured passes away during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium guarantee ensures financial predictability over the term, enabling the policyholder to maintain coverage without cost shocks; this stability facilitates potential reinstatement later, especially since the five-year reinvestment window matches the guaranteed term duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums during the term supports continuous coverage, reducing risk of lapse; however, if a lapse does occur despite this guarantee, reinstatement becomes necessary and depends on paying backlogged premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums during the term ensures predictable cost, whereas the interest charge on past-due amounts applies only if the policy lapses and is later reinstated, adding a potential extra expense outside the guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c51813be-5981-4439-bc82-d2593f62bf3f" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">issues policy with guaranteed level premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7125145f-60f1-4236-b2a8-d6e539de3a54" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">pays guaranteed level premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dda4fe9f-ec01-42f5-a7d9-e62700f5ae65" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has guaranteed rate</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16a529f5-ae10-482a-9029-57548ed48ff5" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has guaranteed level premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="49010202-fde3-476d-98f4-d300347db155">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="7e06d37d-cad7-4701-a273-ebee09a2478e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="84052e93-a85b-41c3-85bc-702b0ae1cd79">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="1f0e2e47-7866-4c38-bcb2-ca613268a55c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="3419c034-c76f-4bc3-bcd6-40e5b1391198">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="cc246f3e-0e6b-4925-9003-4f83244f7e63">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="c807274f-f9be-4d7c-84a8-2a7ae146e382">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="4c07f39e-ad05-4917-95e2-35541c6936c2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="b4f05c14-2b6e-48b2-8628-e9ce0c91b8ee">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="12683029-d44f-41fc-9271-5fdae783b64f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="5a2194b4-5b49-461d-8dbb-cdab2015d91a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="995539a8-9266-4a45-81b8-d491652f25bf">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="a1940a31-c964-4c23-91a5-6b41c8159913">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Since coverage ends upon termination of the term, it underscores why premiums are set at a stable, level amount for the entire guarantee period—to maintain affordability across the known lifespan of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Termination upon expiration of the term implies that ongoing premium payments beyond the initial period require renewal; thus, the stability of those future premiums depends on whether renewal occurs under new terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">If coverage ends at the term’s close, it may only be extended via renewal or conversion under conditions set forth in the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about coverage terminating at the end of the term relies on prior definitions establishing what constitutes the policy itself, but does not directly build upon or modify the definition.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term limits the window during which benefits might be payable. However, even within that window, benefits remain contingent upon compliance with policy-specific terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that coverage ends unless renewed, implying continuation through reissuance under new terms. Fact_sentence_2 specifies that coverage ends unless converted into another type of policy, suggesting a structural change rather than simple extension. Both address post-term outcomes using alternative triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The policy's coverage duration ends upon expiration of the term, but it only applies to the specific individual designated as the Insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is only available if the policy remains active; since coverage ends at the term's conclusion unless renewed, the benefit ceases to apply beyond that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder fails to pay the required premium, coverage will terminate at the end of the term. Therefore, timely premium payments are essential to sustain coverage through the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">necessitates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">If coverage expires at the end of the term without renewal, the Death Benefit ceases to apply because the policy is no longer in force. Therefore, the Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy remaining active throughout the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The policy continues in force during the grace period despite the upcoming end of the term, allowing time for renewal or premium payment without immediate lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage for up to 31 days after a missed premium, preventing immediate lapse even if the term is nearing its end. This interim protection ensures flexibility without altering the final termination date.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">If coverage expires at the end of the term without renewal, the policy may become inactive, creating a scenario where reinstatement could apply to revive it.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term provides the temporal boundary within which the incontestability period operates, ensuring that challenges to policy validity occur only during its active phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term relies on the policy's immutable nature; since no one can change its provisions, the expiration date remains binding without exception.</data>
  <data key="d4">ensures</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term relies on the policy’s legal foundation, which is established through accurate representations in the application. Without truthful disclosure, the policy might not have been issued, affecting its duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">If coverage is not renewed by the end of the term, it ceases; however, renewal requires timely payment of all upcoming premiums, ensuring continuity only if obligations are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage after the five-year term relies on the prior establishment of the policy through the payment of the first premium. Without this initial payment, the coverage would never begin, rendering its expiration moot.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">Coverage begins precisely at 12:01 A.M. Standard Time on the Effective Date, setting the initial point from which the five-year term operates before terminating.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term may affect the exercise of rights by the Policy Owner, who controls the policy’s fate post-term through potential renewal or lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">Coverage expiration occurs after the five-year term concludes if renewal does not happen, marking the endpoint of protection. This outcome depends on knowing when the policy began, which is established by the Effective Date found on the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term occurs regardless of the examination period, but the 20-day right to examine allows the insured to assess and possibly void the policy before it becomes binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
