</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The concept of the policy relies on identifying who is covered; thus, specifying the Insured completes the fundamental identity of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the Insured—someone whose life is covered—is established within the overall documentation package that constitutes the policy, including forms and endorsements.</data>
  <data key="d4">included in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The Insured is the individual whose life is protected by the policy, and this designation directly determines who triggers the payout mechanism when deceased. Consequently, the Beneficiary is named specifically to receive the Death Benefit upon the Insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The Insured's identity is foundational to triggering the Death Benefit, as the benefit is specifically paid upon the Insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the Insured determines eligibility and conditions for the Death Benefit payout, making it central to how the benefit is applied under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Insured establishes who benefits from the policy’s protection; this role necessitates regular payments, known as premiums, to sustain that coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">needs premium</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Insured establishes the individual whose life is protected by the policy, creating the foundational subject matter for any related policy mechanics, including the Grace Period that preserves coverage after a missed payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Insured establishes the individual protected by the policy, making the Grace Period relevant as a safeguard ensuring continued coverage for that specific person even if payments are delayed.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Insured establishes the subject of coverage, which directly determines the applicability of the incontestability clause that limits the company’s right to dispute the policy during a specified timeframe after issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Insured establishes the individual subject to the policy’s coverage and potential contestation. This creates the necessary context for the company to challenge claims if false information was provided by the insured at application.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the Insured is central to the policy’s issuance, as the insurer evaluates risk and determines coverage based on the applicant’s declarations in the application.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Insured provides essential context for determining when coverage starts, ensuring that the effective date applies specifically to the correct individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The Insured is the individual protected by the policy; however, this protection remains active only if premiums are paid promptly, ensuring continuous validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 defines who is insured under the policy, establishing the subject of coverage. This context helps explain why the Policy Owner holds contractual rights, as they manage a policy covering a specific individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">Knowing who the Insured is enables determination of ownership if no separate Owner is designated. Without identifying the Insured, the default ownership provision cannot be applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The Insured is the individual covered by the policy, while the Policy Owner holds administrative rights including the power to designate or modify beneficiaries. This reflects how ownership enables certain decision-making powers related to benefit distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Insured is the individual whose life is insured under the policy, and the Owner holds the legal authority to review it, particularly during the mandatory 20-day examination window.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Insured provides context for who is protected by the policy during the 20-day examination window, allowing the policyholder to assess whether the coverage aligns with their intended beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
