  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="0571a1f4-a9e4-435f-a1ee-9ba4578ac963">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Since the Death Benefit is subject to policy terms and exclusions, the designation of the Beneficiary must align with those constraints to ensure validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit only if the Insured dies, making the identity and status of the Insured essential for activating the benefit transfer process.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit, but its availability and amount are constrained by the policy's governing terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is the recipient of the Death Benefit after the Insured's passing, which is paid out only if the policy remains active—requiring ongoing premium payments to sustain it.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary receives the Death Benefit when the Insured dies; this role only has meaning if the Death Benefit is established as a payable sum.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary receives the death benefit upon the insured's passing, but this payout could be challenged if the company discovers material misrepresentations during underwriting.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary's right to receive the Death Benefit is determined by the documents included in the Entire Contract, including the policy itself and any amendments.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary's entitlement to the Death Benefit relies on accurate disclosures during application, ensuring legitimacy and validity of claims. Without truthful application data, even properly named beneficiaries may face denial.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary's right to receive the Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy being properly issued, which requires the initial premium payment described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The designation of a Beneficiary relies on the policy remaining in force, which requires ongoing premium payments. Without timely payments, the policy lapses, nullifying the beneficiary's right to the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is determined by the insured party but requires authorization through the policy owner, who controls changes to beneficiary status.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit when the Insured passes away, while the Policy Owner has control over the policy, including the ability to name or change beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit after the insured passes away, but only if the policy was active at that time. Coverage beginning at 12:01 A.M. on the Effective Date ensures the policy is live before any potential payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="80518b2d-1bb2-4fa2-93b9-79573d720a98">
  <data key="d3">The general definition of a beneficiary provided in fact_sentence_2 helps clarify the significance of the individuals listed in fact_sentence_1 who are set to receive the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="90ec6e29-a29c-4e3c-8d1b-c21dc571dc89">
  <data key="d3">The general definition of "Beneficiary" in fact_sentence_2 clarifies the role fulfilled by Elaine M. Hughes as specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="d13623e0-a45f-4060-82e1-dbdfcb46c827">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 offers foundational terminology that helps interpret the roles described in fact_sentence_1, particularly regarding the designation of Morgan L. Hughes as the contingent beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
