<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">If the policy expires at the end of its term without renewal, the Death Benefit becomes irrelevant because coverage has terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is designed to be paid when the insured dies, but only if the policy has not yet terminated due to expiration of the term. Therefore, the timing of coverage expiry directly affects whether the benefit becomes applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Death Benefit relies on the broader rule that all benefits are bound by the policy’s terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the Death Benefit as a primary feature of the policy, reinforcing why the definition of “Policy” matters—it governs how benefits are distributed. This makes the role of the policy clear in delivering the promised payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit represents the payout due under the policy when the insured passes away. This element is contained within the broader set of materials that define the complete policy, including schedules and riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">included in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit exists precisely because of the Insured—it is the financial obligation triggered by the Insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is defined by its purpose—to be paid to the Beneficiary after the Insured's death, making the designation of beneficiary essential to its function.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is only paid if the policy remains in force, which requires regular premium payments to maintain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, defined as the sum paid to the beneficiary after the insured's death, is constrained by the specific rules and limitations set forth within the policy itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit represents the insured's promised payout, contingent on maintaining active coverage. The Grace Period helps preserve coverage after a missed premium, thereby preserving eligibility for the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit depends on the policy remaining active; during the grace period, the policy stays in effect, ensuring the death benefit can still be claimed even if a payment is delayed.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent on the policy remaining valid during the Incontestability Period; if contested successfully within this window, the beneficiary might not receive the stated amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is the sum paid to the beneficiary after the insured's passing, and its enforceability is subject to the Incontestability Period, which prevents challenges by the insurer after two years from policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit's validity depends on the policy remaining unaltered; if agents could modify it arbitrarily, the promised payout would lack certainty.</data>
  <data key="d4">ensures</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is the sum paid to the beneficiary after the insured's death, but this payment may be contested by the company if material misrepresentations were found in the original application.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is a key provision explicitly covered under the policy documents comprising the Entire Contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">included in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy being active, which requires the first premium to have been paid. Without the initial payment, the benefit would not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is contingent upon the accuracy of the applicant’s representations during the underwriting process, ensuring the insurer has reliable risk assessment data before committing to pay out the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy remaining active, which requires ongoing premium payments. Without timely payments, the benefit would not be paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined by the policy terms and becomes applicable from the Effective Date listed on the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent on the insured's passing after coverage has begun; therefore, its applicability depends on the effective start time established by the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined and controlled by the Policy Owner, who holds exclusive rights to manage its disbursement and related policy actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">managed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit determines the financial payout to the designated beneficiary after the insured's passing. Since the policy owner controls beneficiary changes, they indirectly influence who ultimately receives this payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is a key component of the policy that the Owner may evaluate during the 20-day examination period to ensure alignment with expectations.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit remains applicable only if the policy is actively maintained or successfully reinstated after lapse. Without reinstatement within five years, the Death Benefit becomes unpayable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit remains enforceable only if the policy is actively maintained; reinstatement after lapse ensures continued validity of the Death Benefit through repayment of overdue premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is only payable if the policy remains active; reinstatement allows restoration of coverage after lapsing, making it essential for maintaining eligibility for the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the Death Benefit as the payment owed upon the insured’s death; fact_sentence_2 explains that this payment occurs only after verified proof of death is submitted while the policy is active.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is only payable after verified proof of death, including a certified death certificate, confirming eligibility for the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="80518b2d-1bb2-4fa2-93b9-79573d720a98">
  <data key="d3">The concept of the Death Benefit—defined in fact_sentence_2—is concretely realized in chunk_summary_1 through the specified $500,000 face amount of the policy owned by Jordan Everett Hughes.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="90ec6e29-a29c-4e3c-8d1b-c21dc571dc89">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit referenced in fact_sentence_2 directly applies to the primary beneficiary, Elaine M. Hughes, whose entitlement is specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="d13623e0-a45f-4060-82e1-dbdfcb46c827">
  <data key="d3">The concept of the Death Benefit directly supports the significance of naming Morgan L. Hughes as the contingent beneficiary, ensuring clarity about what she may inherit upon the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="af0642b0-b73b-4d5a-941d-8b8a65fef5d4">
  <data key="d3">A guaranteed level premium structure enables reliable payment of the Death Benefit, making it feasible for the insurer to meet its contractual obligations under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75" target="dc7d257a-6a88-40ef-9995-0d6cef3ac4dd">
  <data key="d3">The concept of a Death Benefit underscores why premium stability matters—it ensures the promised payout can be delivered without interruption due to cost increases.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
