<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Understanding that a premium maintains policy validity explains why insurers guarantee stable, unchanging premiums throughout the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums must be paid to keep the policy active, the assurance that they won't rise during the term provides financial predictability and strengthens the appeal of maintaining coverage under stable conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay a premium ensures continued coverage; without it, the policy would expire when the term ends, leading to loss of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">Regular premium payments are essential to sustain coverage during the term, ensuring the policy does not terminate prematurely or upon expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The need to pay a premium ensures continued eligibility for renewal or conversion options specified within the policy agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Without timely premium payments, the policy may lapse, thereby preventing beneficiaries from receiving death benefits despite the existence of those benefits in principle.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for regular Premiums ensures the ongoing validity of the Policy, making them essential operational elements of the same legal instrument.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">Regular premium payments ensure the continued existence of the policy, thereby preserving the protection afforded to the Insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables coverage</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">Premiums ensure the policy stays in effect so that the designated Beneficiary can ultimately receive the Death Benefit when the Insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Regular premium payments ensure that the policy stays active, enabling the Death Benefit to be paid upon the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Premiums are necessary to sustain the policy’s validity, ensuring that the promised Death Benefit remains enforceable under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">If a premium is not paid on time, the policy enters a grace period during which coverage remains active despite the delinquency.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Payment of the Premium ensures continued policy coverage; if not paid on time, the policy may lapse unless maintained via the Grace Period.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, making reinstatement necessary. Reinstatement allows restoration of coverage after lapsation, contingent upon satisfying past-due premium requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">Payment of premiums maintains active policy status over time, enabling the incontestability period to begin once the policy has been in effect for two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums to maintain coverage is grounded in the legal definition of the Entire Contract, which specifies the official components governing policy terms and obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums to maintain coverage relies on the policy's immutable nature; since no one can alter the terms, the premium obligation remains fixed and binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">ensures</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums ensures ongoing policy protection; failure to do so results in loss of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay a premium ensures the policy remains active; without it, the policy would lapse. This policy was only issued after the first premium was paid, confirming its initiation hinges on this financial obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The obligation to pay premiums arises because the policy was issued based on the applicant’s representations; without truthful disclosures, the policy might not have been approved or could be voided.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">Premiums ensure the policy remains active so that coverage can commence on the designated effective date. Without payment, the policy would lapse before coverage begins.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums ensures the policy remains active, and since the Policy Owner holds all contractual rights, they are accountable for making these payments to preserve the policy’s effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d4">responsible for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Premiums sustain the policy's active status; therefore, the policy owner’s right to cancel relies on recognizing that discontinuing payments ends coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">Premiums ensure ongoing coverage, while the owner's examination right allows them to assess policy terms prior to commitment, potentially influencing their decision to pay premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay a premium ensures ongoing coverage, and the 20-day examination period provides a safeguard allowing the policyholder to assess whether they wish to proceed with making those payments after reviewing the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="328f68c5-301e-4d5f-8323-57ff947dd2fd" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">pays</data>
</edge>
