<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement refers to restoring a lapsed policy, but this option is restricted to a maximum of 5 years after lapse, as specified in the instatement period.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a reinstatement option implies that policies can lapse, including those terminating at the end of their initial term when not renewed.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of reinstating a lapsed policy depends on whether coverage has already expired—such as at the end of the term—and thus applies only after termination events outlined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy depends on meeting specific criteria set forth in the policy’s terms; thus, any successful reinstatement would still fall under the broader rule that benefits are subject to policy-defined limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The concept of reinstatement applies only to existing policies, making clear reference to the existence and nature of a policy—a point established in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy depends on the insurer's authority and procedures, which are governed by Sentinel Life Assurance Company’s underwriting and operational standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">managed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires action from the Owner, who holds the legal authority to restore it to active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement requires meeting conditions including paying overdue premiums; thus, it directly relies on the concept that premiums are essential to maintaining policy status.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement depends on the prior occurrence of a missed premium followed by expiration of the grace period. Without the grace period providing a delay, reinstatement would not apply since the policy could have already been terminated earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses because the Grace Period expired without payment, reinstatement becomes the mechanism through which the insured can regain active coverage by fulfilling required conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy involves restoring its active status under specific conditions; however, this process cannot override the rule that no agent may change policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement allows a lapsed policy to become active again, but any modification during that process would still require official written consent per company rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement allows a lapsed policy to become active again only if all outstanding premiums are paid promptly. Without timely payment of premiums, reinstatement cannot occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires the policy owner's authorization, as they hold exclusive control over contractual actions. Without ownership rights, the reinstatement process cannot proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement allows a previously lapsed policy to become active again, but if the policy owner chooses to cancel the policy entirely, reinstatement becomes irrelevant. This describes how cancellation supersedes any attempt at restoration.</data>
  <data key="d4">suppresses</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement allows a lapsed policy to become active again, which could occur after the owner exercises their right to examine the policy and decides to take corrective action. This implies that the examination period precedes potential reinstatement actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy depends on having a legally recognized Owner; since the Insured automatically becomes the Owner without a named party, they hold the necessary authority to initiate reinstatement procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy depends on timely action; however, the 20-day examination window provides an opportunity to cancel the policy entirely before it becomes binding, thus preventing lapsation altogether.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">The first statement describes reinstatement as a legitimate method to restore a lapsed policy’s active status, but the second asserts that returning the policy renders it void from its beginning, negating any potential for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">The ability to return the policy within 20 days for a full refund provides an exit option prior to commitment, whereas reinstatement allows revival after lapse, offering recovery only under specific conditions. These features represent complementary safeguards—one enabling cancellation without penalty, the other permitting renewal after failure to pay.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy (fact_sentence_1) relies on formal documentation, as required by the rule that no policy change is valid without written consent (fact_sentence_2).</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy (fact_sentence_1) relies on formal written approval from an authorized company officer, as required by policy rules (fact_sentence_2).</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores a lapsed policy, but treating it as "never issued" suggests a complete legal reset rather than continuation, implying potential conflict in interpretation.</data>
  <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
