<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The two-year incontestability period exemplifies a specific term that governs when and how benefits can be contested, aligning with the overarching condition stated in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The Incontestability Period ensures that once two years have passed since policy issuance, the insurer cannot dispute the validity of the claim regarding the Death Benefit, thereby protecting the beneficiary's right to receive it.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The two-year incontestability period ensures that after its expiration, the Death Benefit becomes fully enforceable unless fraud is proven.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">After two years from policy inception, the incontestability period begins, ensuring that failure to pay premiums does not invalidate benefits if death occurs later.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The two-year Incontestability Period sets the time frame during which the insurance company retains the right to dispute the policy's validity based on inaccuracies in the application.</data>
  <data key="d4">defines window</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The two-year incontestability period establishes the timeframe during which the insurer can challenge the policy due to material misrepresentations made at application.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Incontestability Period establishes a timeframe within which insurers cannot challenge policy validity due to misstatements; this limitation applies specifically to the documents included in the Entire Contract, ensuring clarity about what is legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period starts after the policy is issued, which requires the payment of the first premium. Without the first premium, the policy—and thus the incontestability period—does not begin.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period limits the insurer’s ability to dispute coverage due to inaccuracies in the application after two years from issuance. This ensures that once the policy has been active for two years, the insured or beneficiary can rely on its validity regardless of prior application errors.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The Incontestability Period starts upon the Effective Date of the policy, meaning its duration depends on when coverage officially begins. This temporal connection allows the two facts to be interpreted together within the timeline of the policy’s lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
