</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the incontestability period limits when the company can dispute the policy’s validity, thereby affecting how long the insured remains protected from retroactive denial despite potential issues discovered post-issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">If the company contests the policy during the incontestability period, any benefit payments may be withheld or denied due to invalidity, even though benefits normally follow policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period applies specifically to the policy described in fact_sentence_1; thus, knowing the nature of the policy enables interpretation of how long the insurer can challenge its validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The Company’s power to contest policy validity during the incontestability period assumes its identity as the issuer, established in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The existence of an incontestability period depends on identifying the Insured, as this provision only governs challenges to the policy based on information related to the individual whose life is insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The company’s right to contest the policy’s validity limits the certainty of the Death Benefit being paid, making the existence of the death benefit dependent on successful underwriting validation over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is invalidated during the incontestability period, the Death Benefit becomes unenforceable, making the timing of challenges critical to benefit eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The company’s authority to contest the policy’s validity is restricted to the initial two-year Incontestability Period after issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">falls in period</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period limits when the insurer can dispute the policy’s validity, while the entire contract clause specifies which documents form the binding agreement; together, they define boundaries of enforceability and documentation scope.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The Incontestability Period grants the insurer authority to challenge the policy’s validity, but only if there were material misrepresentations made at application. Without such misrepresentations, the company cannot contest the policy even within this period.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period enables the insurer to challenge the policy based on misrepresentations in the application. This right exists because the policy was issued contingent upon accurate information from the applicant.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes the insurer’s right to dispute policy validity within a specific timeframe. This limitation supports the broader rule stated in fact sentence 2—that no unauthorized changes can be made to the policy, preserving its original form.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period defines when the company can legally dispute the policy’s validity due to misrepresented information; however, this right does not apply until the policy is formally issued, which requires the initial premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
