  <data key="d3">Any attempt to modify the terms governing benefits—including exclusions—depends on adherence to the procedural safeguard specified in fact_sentence_2, directly linking it to the scope of benefits established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt to alter the Policy—as defined in the prior statement—requires explicit written approval from a company officer, ensuring control over contractual modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires authorization</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">Any change to parts of the policy—including its application, schedule, or riders—must be authorized through explicit written consent from a company officer, reflecting the boundaries established by the policy’s composition.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer implies institutional control over policy changes, reinforcing the legal entity responsible—Sentinel Life Assurance Company—as central to enforcement and modification procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">Any change to the policy requires explicit written approval by the company, reflecting the limits on even fully owned rights to prevent unilateral actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt to alter the Death Benefit must follow formal procedures involving written authorization from a company officer, ensuring compliance with the original policy framework governing the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">Any change to the policy’s terms—including those involved in reinstatement—requires explicit written authorization from a company officer.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">Since alterations to the Entire Contract require explicit written consent, this rule reinforces the boundaries established by defining what comprises the contract itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer enforces the rule that no one else—including agents—may change the policy, reinforcing the binding nature of the original agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization ensures that modifications to the policy cannot occur without official consent, preserving the integrity of the agreement grounded in the applicant’s original statements.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization ensures that while the policy owner holds all contractual rights, they cannot unilaterally alter the policy without official approval, preserving the integrity of the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change beneficiaries is subject to the condition that any such change must be formally authorized in writing by the company, ensuring compliance with contractual procedures.</data>
