<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of premiums enables the policyholder to exercise the right to reinstate the policy within the 5-year post-lapse window.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments are necessary to sustain coverage, relying on the assurance that amounts owed remain unchanged across the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments are essential for ongoing coverage, and since premiums do not increase during the term, this requirement remains consistent and manageable over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of premiums enables continued coverage past the original term, preventing automatic termination upon expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments are essential to maintain active coverage; failure to pay results in automatic termination at the end of the term, rendering any intention to extend ineffective.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments enable the maintenance of coverage, which is necessary to qualify for future renewal or conversion under the policy’s stipulated conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums on time undermines the conditions necessary for any benefits to be paid out, reinforcing the limitation imposed by the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments are required to maintain the validity of the policy, which was established as the core contractual agreement under the specified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of premiums, as stated in fact_sentence_2, is essential for maintaining the validity of the policy’s components listed in fact_sentence_1; failure to meet this condition may result in lapse despite having those elements present.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of premiums ensures ongoing coverage under the policy issued by Sentinel Life Assurance Company, reinforcing the role of the insurer in maintaining contractual obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments sustain coverage for the Insured, meaning the obligation to pay ensures the definition of "Insured" retains its protective effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments are required to sustain coverage, which is essential because only the Owner has the right to manage and preserve the policy through consistent contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments ensure continuous coverage, enabling the insured’s designated Beneficiary to ultimately receive the Death Benefit as specified in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments ensure the policy remains in force, thereby preserving the right to receive the Death Benefit specified in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments ensure continued coverage, which is necessary for the Death Benefit to remain active and applicable at the time of the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments are essential to sustain coverage, directly reflecting the purpose of a premium as outlined in the definition.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of all future premiums ensures that coverage remains active even after missing one—this condition makes the grace period meaningful only when followed by prompt resumption of payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of premiums is essential to sustain coverage; without it, even if the grace period initially preserves the policy’s status, continuation becomes impossible.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of premiums is essential because it determines whether a lapsed policy can be successfully reinstated and returned to active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments ensure continuation of coverage governed by the Entire Contract, which legally binds the insurer and insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments are essential for ongoing coverage, and since no agent can waive this obligation, the requirement remains strictly enforced as written.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments sustain the policy’s active status, reflecting adherence to the agreement established during issuance. This requirement stems directly from the applicant’s representations in the original application, which justified the policy’s approval and pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of all premiums beyond the first is required to maintain coverage, implying that the initial premium was necessary but not sufficient alone—ongoing compliance ensures continuation. Thus, the requirement for continuous payments stems from the foundational act of paying the first premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for continued coverage based on premium payments only applies after coverage has begun. Without a clear start point established by the effective date, the obligation to maintain premiums lacks temporal context.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payment ensures ongoing coverage, but only if the party with control—the Policy Owner—fulfills this obligation. Without the Owner managing payments, continuation of coverage cannot occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payment ensures active coverage, but the policy owner may still choose to terminate the policy regardless of payment history by exercising the cancellation right.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments ensure continuous protection under the policy, while the Owner’s right to examine the policy allows them to verify its terms before committing further. This inspection opportunity enables informed decisions regarding renewal or continuation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79b163e1-cff6-49a9-9651-6f45e3b01614" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is required to make</data>
</edge>
