  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The Owner’s ability to assign the policy presupposes that coverage is active, meaning the assignment only applies after the policy takes effect at 12:01 A.M. on the Effective Date.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">Because the Policy Owner holds all contractual rights, they inherently possess the ability to assign the policy, making this action a natural extension of their full ownership status.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy enables transfer of ownership interests, which includes the subsequent ability to designate new beneficiaries through the new owner, making it logically connected to changing beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to assign the policy demonstrates control over its transfer, which complements their power to initiate cancellation, reflecting comprehensive ownership autonomy.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy belongs to the designated Policy Owner; if no Owner is specified, the Insured automatically assumes that role.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional right</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Owner’s ability to assign the policy depends on first having access to its contents, which is enabled by the examination right. This ensures informed decisions before transferring ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s broader authority to manage its transfer, which inherently includes changing the beneficiary, reinforcing the owner’s control over distribution of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s broader capacity to manage ownership transfers, which complements the ability to change beneficiaries independently, ensuring consistent control over policy disposition.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to assign the policy supports their broader authority to manage ownership transfers, which includes changing beneficiaries independently through formal requests.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 grants the Policy Owner the broad right to assign the policy, which is further clarified in fact_sentence_2 through detailed procedures requiring a written assignment approved by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">elaborates on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy underscores the owner’s broad control, enabling them to transfer ownership entirely—a capability consistent with the authority to unilaterally change beneficiaries, even posthumously.</data>
  <data key="d4">complementary rights</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy underscores the policy owner’s broad control over its disposition, which complements the separate but related right to unilaterally change beneficiaries without requiring the insured’s consent or presence.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s comprehensive control, enabling them to transfer it before cancellation; this complements the explicit right to cancel at any time.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy depends on having access to its documentation; thus, the ability to request a copy supports the enforcement of assignment rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports transparency needs, making it relevant that the owner can also request premium payment history to verify the policy’s financial standing before transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">complementary rights</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s broader capacity to manage beneficiary designations, as assignment may transfer these responsibilities to another party. This ensures continuity of intent even after ownership changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s ability to transfer control, which can be exercised when adding riders like the Accelerated Death Benefit. This enhances flexibility in managing the policy post-transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79d7c579-6c3e-45f4-9ba4-aa81ddab7b31" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has right to assign policy</data>
</edge>
