<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">If no owner is designated, the insured automatically becomes the owner, thereby gaining eligibility for the 20-day examination window.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">The default assignment of ownership to the insured enables them to exercise the 20-day right to review and return the policy without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The default designation of the insured as owner sets a baseline condition that may later be changed only via written agreement, ensuring procedural integrity in ownership transitions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">When no owner is named, the insured becomes the legal owner by default, granting them authority over the policy—including the right to exercise the 20-day examination period and request a full refund if dissatisfied.</data>
  <data key="d4">defaults to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">When no owner is named, the insured becomes the owner by default, granting them the right to review and return the policy within the examination window. Returning the policy results in its cancellation retroactively from the start date.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The default assignment of ownership to the insured provides a foundation for control over the policy, ensuring that only authorized personnel—such as official company representatives—can make modifications, thereby maintaining integrity and preventing unauthorized actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">If no owner is named, the insured becomes the owner, enabling them to initiate actions like returning the policy. Returning the policy results in its treatment as if never issued, effectively nullifying the contract regardless of prior ownership status.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The default assignment of ownership to the insured enables them to exercise rights such as initiating policy reinstatement, which may trigger exceptions to benefit termination. This creates a potential pathway for recovery of benefits despite lapsation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="4c454305-8df7-4f9a-b113-fd49d2e08142">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 provides a critical interpretive framework for understanding who controls the policy; in this case, since no owner is listed, Jordan Hughes is legally considered the owner, which aligns with the terms outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The rule assigning ownership to the insured in absence of a named owner enables them to exercise the 20-day right to examine the policy and request cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The rule assigning ownership to the Insured when unassigned provides necessary legal standing to manage the policy—including utilizing the 31-day grace period—making it foundational for activating the grace period provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility hinges on the Owner's capacity to act; if the Owner is not explicitly named, the Insured assumes that role, enabling them to restore the policy under applicable conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The rule that the insured becomes owner by default supports the ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within 5 years, ensuring the rightful party can act on behalf of the policy during the reinstatement period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The first statement defines who holds ownership by default, which grants the authority to initiate actions like changing beneficiaries. This foundational role supports the validity of the second statement regarding timely implementation of beneficiary requests.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The default assignment of ownership to the insured ensures that the individual has the legal authority to make binding decisions like changing beneficiaries, even if not explicitly stated otherwise.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Without a designated owner, the insured becomes the default owner, enabling them to initiate beneficiary changes per fact_sentence_2. This creates a foundational condition allowing the owner’s rights to be exercised.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">When no owner is named, the insured becomes the default owner, granting them the legal authority to make decisions such as changing the beneficiary, as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
