<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination right exists specifically for the owner; therefore, the assignment of ownership via default rules ensures that this right is available to the insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">The owner's right to review the policy for 20 days enables them to assess its terms and decide whether to proceed. If they find the policy unacceptable within this period, they have the option to return it.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">The owner’s 20-day examination right enables them to review the policy and decide whether to keep it. If they choose not to proceed, returning the policy within this timeframe triggers a full refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">If the owner chooses not to proceed with the policy within the 20-day examination period, they can return it, resulting in the policy being nullified retroactively from its start date.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">If the owner chooses not to proceed with the policy within the 20-day examination period, returning it triggers its treatment as voided.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination right allows the owner to review the policy before commitment, and this right remains enforceable only because any changes to its conditions must be formally documented in writing.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The owner’s 20-day examination right enables them to review the policy terms thoroughly, ensuring awareness before committing; however, even during this period, no unauthorized party—including agents or brokers—can make changes, preserving contractual integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination right enables the owner to assess the policy's terms before commitment, ensuring informed decision-making prior to any financial obligation. This initial evaluation window precedes the start of regular premium responsibilities, including the subsequent 31-day grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination window allows the owner to assess the policy terms before committing financially. If they fail to make a timely premium payment during the subsequent 31-day grace period, the policy loses its benefit protection entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="4c454305-8df7-4f9a-b113-fd49d2e08142">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of the application and riders as integral parts of the contract enables the enforcement of the 20-day inspection window, allowing the owner to assess all binding terms prior to finalizing acceptance.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 assigns the examination right to the Owner, which aligns with fact_sentence_1’s assertion that the right exists for 20 days from receipt, thereby contextualizing who can use the stated privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination right gives the owner a chance to reject the policy before binding commitments, whereas the 31-day grace period offers flexibility after a missed premium, ensuring continuity without immediate lapse due to timing issues.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination period enables the owner to avoid future need for reinstatement by terminating the policy early, thereby eliminating the risk of lapse that would trigger reinstatement procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination right supports informed decision-making prior to binding obligations, making it easier to avoid lapses and thus increasing the likelihood of successfully utilizing the subsequent 5-year reinstatement option.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
