<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day right to return the policy and receive a full refund implies that whoever holds ownership during this window—the insured by default—is empowered to act on it, reinforcing the significance of the default ownership rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">entitles to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy within 20 days results in a full refund, which only applies because the policy grants the owner a 20-day examination period to evaluate its terms before commitment.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">A full refund of premiums is issued when the policy is returned within 20 days, contingent upon the owner's dissatisfaction with the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy within 20 days triggers a full refund and causes the policy to be voided effective from its start date.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy within 20 days results in a full refund, and under such circumstances, the policy is legally considered not to have been issued at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day refund window depends on the policy remaining unaltered, reinforcing why only authorized personnel can make changes to ensure compliance with refund eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day refund window applies only when procedures are followed correctly; this ensures that even though agents cannot override rules, legitimate claims like early returns remain enforceable through formal channels.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces limitation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day refund right applies when the policy is returned early, but any modification to this rule would need formal approval from the insurer’s authorized personnel.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="4c454305-8df7-4f9a-b113-fd49d2e08142">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a conditional refund right within 20 days of receiving the policy, which complements fact_sentence_1 by clarifying one of the administrative procedures included in the overall contract package.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains what happens when the 20-day examination period ends, clarifying the benefit associated with the right mentioned in fact_sentence_1. It operationalizes the examination right through the refund mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">A 20-day examination period permits policyholders to cancel and get a full refund, preventing financial loss from premature decisions. Reinstatement offers a later opportunity to restore coverage after lapse, contingent on fulfilling requirements like paying overdue premiums and passing medical review.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day refund provision enables withdrawal without obligation early on, while the 5-year reinstatement rule permits revival later—these features together support flexible exit and re-entry options under differing conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ebffabe4-cca1-4619-9aea-7f2dec353e08" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has right to refund</data>
</edge>
<edge source="908a8f02-87b7-405f-8415-8530255bd829" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">provides refund under condition</data>
</edge>
