<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy leads to it being treated as if never issued, meaning that even if the insured was previously considered the owner due to lack of designation, this status becomes irrelevant once the policy is canceled under this provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires owner</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination right allows the owner to cancel the policy by returning it, resulting in it being considered never issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">The policy being treated as if never issued results from the owner exercising their right to return it within the 20-day examination period.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">The policy's status as if never issued means that any financial obligations, like premium payments, are fully reversed through a complete refund when returned within the examination period.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 explains that returning the policy results in treating it as nonexistent. This condition matches exactly what fact sentence 1 describes by stating the policy is void from inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">equivalent to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy results in it being nullified as though it was never issued, emphasizing the importance of documented actions when modifying or canceling policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is returned, it is voided as though not issued; this outcome relies on the restriction that only authorized personnel can make changes, preventing unauthorized alterations prior to issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">If a policy is returned, it is treated as if never issued, underscoring the importance of maintaining contractual integrity. No agent or broker can override this rule through waiver, ensuring consistent enforcement across all cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is returned, it is treated as though never issued, but this rule does not apply when reinstatement terms are met, allowing benefits to resume despite prior cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy within the 20-day exam period cancels the contract entirely, meaning the policy is considered not issued at any point.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates that returning the policy renders it invalid as though never issued, reinforcing the importance of timely action during the 20-day examination window—before any commitment—including ensuring premium payments begin promptly once accepted.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The claim that a reinstated policy is treated as if never issued undermines the notion of restoration, suggesting a paradoxical outcome where revival negates original validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement beyond 5 years is not permitted; however, returning the policy voids its existence altogether, making reinstatement impossible regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">nullifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="94e5fbba-ba2a-4677-a745-9c9e9423ebb0" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">initiates return</data>
</edge>
