  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that agents and brokers cannot waive policy provisions, which aligns with and strengthens the requirement in fact sentence 1 that only an authorized officer may make changes, ensuring consistent enforcement of policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against waiving policy provisions (sentence 2) reinforces why agents cannot modify policies (sentence 1), as allowing such waivers would undermine formal change procedures requiring written authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
