  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures long-term stability of the policy terms after two years, allowing any inaccuracies like misstated age to still trigger corrective actions such as benefit adjustments without contestation by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">posteriority</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision becomes effective after two years of uninterrupted policy existence, contingent on continued compliance with premium obligations such as those outlined in the grace period rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision applies only if the policy remains active; failing to pay premiums within the grace period terminates benefits and prevents the policyholder from benefiting from the two-year incontestability rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause ensures the insurer cannot challenge claims after two years, while the reinstatement exception allows recovery of benefits despite lapses, providing complementary safeguards for policyholders' rights over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot challenge the validity of the policy due to misrepresentation, while reinstatement requires demonstrating current insurability, reflecting separate safeguards for claim integrity and policy continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="4c454305-8df7-4f9a-b113-fd49d2e08142">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces the incontestability provision effective after two years, which complements fact_sentence_1 by ensuring the contractual obligations—including those involving riders and beneficiaries—are legally enforceable once the waiting period passes.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="0d5e54d4-82aa-4712-9f7e-bdb99dc0e6ca">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2's assertion of incontestability after two years depends on the presence of the suicide exclusion clause described in fact_sentence_1, as such exclusions are standard exceptions to incontestability, particularly concerning suicide-related deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
