<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision after two years assumes the policy remained in force; however, if the policy was returned and voided at inception, this condition cannot be met.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a fixed incontestability period depends on proper documentation; without written consent, altering it would not be legally binding under fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause, effective after two years, reinforces trust in the policy’s permanence, making it less likely that disputes arise over misrepresentations—a condition made more credible by requiring official authorization for any changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision after two years reinforces the need for adherence to formal procedures, ensuring only authorized representatives can effect changes, thus supporting the restriction on agent waivers.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">The second statement refines the first by specifying an important exception: even after two years, the insurer may contest claims due to nonpayment of premiums, thus modifying the blanket incontestability asserted earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause after two years excludes non-payment but does not override the suicide provision, which specifically restricts benefits when death results from suicide within the first two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states the policy becomes incontestable after two years unless due to non-payment; fact_sentence_2 clarifies that material misrepresentations during application can still allow contestation within that period, serving as a critical exception to the general rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="64edfdb5-aded-401b-bbe7-55880fad2b56">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision after two years excludes nonpayment cases, while the suicide clause imposes a separate limitation on death benefits within the same timeframe, ensuring insurers cannot be challenged over misrepresentations when suicide occurs early, even though the policy may otherwise become incontestable.</data>
  <data key="d4">exempted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="fffa6d30-0053-4c00-b207-2a77ad194bd2">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes that the policy becomes incontestable after two years, barring non-payment issues. This provides a foundational protection that indirectly contextualizes the second sentence, which limits payouts due to suicide within the same initial two-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">temporal context</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures the insurer cannot challenge the policy's validity after two years, reinforcing the benefit of the 31-day grace period by enabling uninterrupted coverage progression toward that milestone.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision becomes effective after two years, ensuring long-term stability of benefits, while the grace period allows temporary continuation of coverage post-due date without immediate lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause after two years does not apply if a premium is not paid; therefore, failure to pay within the grace period leads to policy lapse, which prevents the application of incontestability rights related to non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision excludes nonpayment scenarios; therefore, if a premium isn't paid during the grace period, the policy terminates, making it subject to cancellation without contestation under the stated condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision after two years excludes cases where premiums were not paid; therefore, if a premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, the policyholder loses all benefits, making the exclusion enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause ensures long-term stability of the policy's validity after two years, supporting the feasibility of reinstatement options later on. This provides legal grounding for exceptions to benefit termination through formal reactivation procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision protects against future disputes after two years, enabling greater confidence in maintaining coverage. This indirectly supports the ability to reinstate a lapsed policy by reducing uncertainty about claim validity during reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision protects the policyholder by preventing future challenges to the policy’s validity after two years, unless due to unpaid premiums. This creates a stable foundation that allows for potential reinstatement later, contingent on new underwriting standards like those required in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">independently related</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d73a02c-fb33-43fa-978b-50c805f978e6" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has incontestability right after two years from effective date</data>
</edge>
