  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">A policy may be voided due to material misrepresentation within two years, emphasizing the importance of ensuring all changes are formally documented in writing to maintain enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a time-limited condition under which false information can void the policy; this justifies the requirement in fact_sentence_1 that any modification must be officially documented, ensuring such changes cannot circumvent liability tied to initial representations.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">If a material misrepresentation occurs, it underscores why only officially authorized individuals should handle policy changes—to prevent fraudulent or erroneous alterations that might compromise the insurer’s ability to assess risk accurately.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentations can nullify the policy within two years; this provision relies on unwaivable rules enforced by the insurer, such as the one preventing agents from overriding policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">If a material misrepresentation was made at application, the insurer retains the right to contest the policy's validity even after two years have passed, thereby overriding the standard incontestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies circumstances—material misrepresentation or omission—that permit the insurer to challenge the policy within two years; this directly limits the scope of fact_sentence_1’s blanket incontestability provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes how material misrepresentation can nullify the policy within two years; this sets a broader legal condition under which the insurer avoids liability. Fact sentence 2 specifies one such scenario—suicide—as a distinct but parallel exception where the insurer limits its obligation to returning premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="64edfdb5-aded-401b-bbe7-55880fad2b56">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines conditions under which a policy may be voided due to fraud, specifically related to misrepresented risks. This condition operates independently but shares a time-bound limitation (two years) with the suicide clause described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">temporal overlap</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="52a31aaf-1af7-416b-8b31-a19b2a5a1510">
  <data key="d3">Misrepresentation of gender constitutes a material misstatement that could void the policy within two years; however, instead of cancellation, the insurer adjusts coverage proportionally to reflect the correct gender-based premium rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="f1888ece-7434-4b7e-aebc-5434189a9e7a">
  <data key="d3">Misstatements about age fall under broader categories of material misrepresentations that could invalidate a policy within two years. However, instead of voiding the contract outright, the policy adjusts benefits proportionally based on corrected age data.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder misrepresented information affecting risk assessment, it might result in the policy being voided; however, should the policy have already lapsed due to such issues, reinstatement would still depend on providing acceptable evidence of current insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional precedence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
