  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 outlines a specific case (suicide within two years) where the insurer pays only returned premiums instead of the full death benefit. This situation falls under the general principle stated in fact sentence 1—that risks misrepresented at inception may invalidate benefits, especially when tied to intentional acts like suicide.</data>
  <data key="d4">subsumed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
