<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides leeway for timely premium payment after the initial term, allowing continued coverage even if payment is late. It operates independently of the earlier 20-day examination phase, serving a later stage of policy maintenance rather than pre-commitment review.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period depends on the policy’s formal structure, which prevents unauthorized alterations by agents or brokers.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay premiums without lapsing, helping maintain continuous coverage necessary to eventually meet the two-year threshold required for incontestability.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate policy lapse, ensuring continuity of coverage during that window.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payment without immediate policy lapse, enabling the insurer to deduct unpaid premiums from the death benefit if the insured passes away during this time.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed payment without immediate policy termination; failure to pay during this window results in the policy lapsing effective from the original due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payment without immediate consequences; however, failing to pay by its end triggers automatic termination of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payment without immediate loss of coverage. However, if payment isn't made by the end of this window, the policy loses its benefit entitlements.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay premiums before cancellation, enabling potential future reinstatement. This supports the exception-based reinstatement process by preserving eligibility window.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums, preventing automatic lapse and enabling future reinstatement eligibility if the policyholder acts within the allowed timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums before the policy lapses; if not paid by the end of that period, the policy may become inactive but could later be restored through additional requirements like proving insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows late premium payment without policy termination, setting the stage for potential reinstatement where outstanding interest becomes applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums before the policy lapses, enabling future reinstatement by covering those delinquent amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides time to pay premiums before lapsing; if that fails, reinstatement requires proof of insurability, linking the two clauses temporally and conditionally.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay premiums before the policy lapses, enabling future reinstatement within five years if required. Without the grace period, policies would lapse immediately, making reinstatement impossible.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides temporary relief for late premium payments, enabling policyholders to avoid lapses; however, if that window is missed, reinstatement becomes necessary, requiring payment of all delinquent premiums plus interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to make late premium payments without immediate consequence; failing to do so triggers policy lapse, directly linking the two facts.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period maintains policy in-force status beyond the due date, enabling the insurer to fulfill its obligation to pay the death benefit when proof of death is provided.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures that the policy remains active long enough to allow proper processing of a death claim, thereby enabling the requirement for proof of death to be met when needed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
