<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of policy effectiveness during the grace period underscores why written authorizations are necessary—any extension or action affecting coverage must follow formal processes to maintain legal standing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures ongoing policy effectiveness temporarily, enabling compliance before reaching the point where incontestability applies at the two-year mark.</data>
  <data key="d4">postpones</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">The policy's continuation during the grace period depends on the existence of a defined 31-day extension for premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The policy stays effective throughout the grace period, but failure to pay the premium by its conclusion results in immediate lapse as of the original due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">The policy's continuation during the grace period ensures that coverage remains effective, allowing the insurer to apply the provision where unpaid premiums are deducted from the death benefit if the insured passes away while the policy is still in grace.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The policy stays effective throughout the 31-day grace period, but if the premium remains unpaid at its conclusion, coverage ends abruptly due to nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">terminates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The policy remains effective throughout the grace period, but failure to pay by its end results in termination of benefit eligibility. This creates a direct cause-effect link between missed payment and loss of rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The grace period maintains policy validity temporarily after missed payments, preventing immediate termination; this supports the broader framework enabling later reinstatement even after lapse, thus aligning with the exception-based reactivation allowed by the Reinstatement provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage even when a premium is late, preventing immediate lapse. This allows time before a policy becomes eligible for reinstatement under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures the policy remains effective even after a missed payment, creating a window where reinstatement becomes possible through payment of arrears.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued policy effectiveness even after a missed payment, but once the policy lapses beyond this window, reinstatement requires additional steps such as providing acceptable evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures ongoing policy validity even after missed payments; however, if reinstatement is needed beyond this window, unpaid premiums accrue interest as set by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage temporarily after a missed payment, enabling the policyholder time to rectify delinquency before lapse; this creates a pathway for eventual reinstatement within five years if needed.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage despite late payment, creating a window during which reinstatement can still be pursued before the policy lapses permanently.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued policy effectiveness, allowing the death benefit to be paid even if a premium is late, provided death occurs before the policy lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The first fact establishes that the policy stays effective during the grace period, while the second clarifies that missing the deadline at its conclusion terminates coverage, forming a clear temporal condition for continuation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage despite late payment, but once expired, reinstatement becomes necessary; this requires repayment of overdue premiums with interest, making the second fact dependent on the first’s temporal framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The grace period preserves policy effectiveness, enabling the beneficiary to file a death claim later. Proof of death is required only if the policy was active at time of death, making it dependent on remaining covered during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
