<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The rule about deducting unpaid premiums from the death benefit relies on the principle that only authorized representatives may alter policy conditions, preserving consistency in claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">The rule about deducting unpaid premiums from the death benefit applies specifically when the insured dies during the 31-day grace period established by the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit may be reduced by unpaid premiums when the insured dies during the grace period, it implies that the policy was actively in effect at the time—a key reason why the grace period maintains coverage status.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the unpaid premium reduces the death benefit; however, if the premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, no benefits are payable at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The occurrence of death during the grace period triggers deduction of unpaid premiums from the death benefit only because coverage remains active until the grace period expires. This condition relies on the grace period being in effect, which requires timely payment before its conclusion.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The occurrence of death during the grace period triggers deduction of unpaid premiums from the death benefit, contingent on the policy still being active; however, if the premium remains unpaid beyond the grace period, the policy lapses, nullifying future benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The rule about deducting unpaid premiums from the death benefit during the grace period supports the broader framework allowing policy reinstatement within five years after lapse, ensuring consistent handling of outstanding dues across lifecycle stages.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The rule about deducting unpaid premiums during the grace period modifies the final death benefit amount, which is only disbursed once proper proof of death is provided and the policy remains in effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to provide proof of death ensures eligibility for the death benefit, which may be reduced by unpaid premiums if the insured died during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the unpaid premium is subtracted from the death benefit; however, this only matters if the policy hasn't already lapsed due to missed payment beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The first statement describes how unpaid premiums affect the death benefit if the insured dies during the grace period, while the second outlines the requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest to reinstate a lapsed policy. Together, they highlight financial responsibilities related to delayed premium payments across different stages of policy lifecycle.</data>
