<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">A failed premium payment leading to policy lapse underscores why only official representatives should alter policies—ensuring controlled responses such as reinstatement are properly managed according to established terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring timely premium payment leads to policy lapse if unmet, underscoring why agents cannot bypass such conditions without violating contract integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers consequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium within the 31-day grace period results in policy lapse, thereby preventing the accumulation of the two-year duration required for incontestability under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium by the end of the grace period results in policy lapse, thereby triggering the exclusion from incontestability under the two-year rule specifically tied to non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers exclusion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the 31-day grace period triggers automatic policy lapse as of the original premium due date, underscoring the importance of timely payment during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium by the end of the grace period causes the policy to lapse retroactively to the due date, nullifying continued coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium by the end of the grace period causes the policy to lapse, meaning it no longer provides coverage—even if the insured died earlier during the grace period, the claim would only apply if the policy was still in force at time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">When a premium remains unpaid past the grace period, the policy officially lapses, resulting in termination of coverage and cessation of any future benefits being available under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, resulting in termination of coverage. This means the policy's active state ends precisely when the grace period expires.</data>
  <data key="d4">equivalent to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to missed premium payment beyond the grace period, it triggers the condition that requires reinstatement through evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is missed past the grace period, the policy lapses, creating a state where reinstatement becomes necessary. Within five years of this lapse, the policyholder may restore coverage through proper procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
