<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium within the 31-day grace period results in termination of benefits, regardless of whether the owner exercised their initial 20-day inspection privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium within the 31-day grace period ends all future benefits. This condition could prompt the policyholder to return the policy, leading to voidance from inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Without written confirmation from an authorized officer, adjustments to the grace period or exceptions to its rules cannot legally occur, preserving the integrity of the deadline defined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium by the end of the grace period results in termination of benefits, underscoring why only authorized personnel can alter terms—any change outside protocol could jeopardize eligibility for continued protection even if technically compliant otherwise.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium within the 31-day grace period triggers termination of benefits, underscoring why only officially authorized representatives can manage policy conditions—no one else can excuse non-compliance through informal agreements.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on authority</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium within the 31-day grace period nullifies future benefits, thereby undermining the potential application of the two-year incontestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium during the grace period nullifies future benefits, which falls under the exception to incontestability stated in the earlier clause regarding nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers exception</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the 31-day grace period leads directly to cessation of all benefits under the policy, making the grace period critical for maintaining coverage continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium before the grace period ends leads directly to the cessation of benefits, implying the grace period serves as a final opportunity to maintain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium by the end of the grace period nullifies all benefits, meaning even if death occurs during the grace period, no payout follows unless the premium is settled.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The absence of future benefits under the policy follows directly from its lapse when a premium is not paid before the grace period ends, confirming the permanent loss of protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The absence of future benefits occurs because the policy's coverage terminates once the grace period expires due to nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">resulting from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The absence of premium payment beyond the grace period typically ends benefits, but the Reinstatement provision allows recovery of those benefits under specific terms, creating a conditional exception.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay during the grace period causes the policy to lapse, creating a condition under which reinstatement becomes possible within five years if eligibility criteria are satisfied.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is unpaid past the grace period, benefits cease; however, the policyholder may still seek reinstatement by providing acceptable evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid during the grace period, the policy loses its benefits. To restore those benefits, the outstanding premiums must be paid, making reinstatement possible.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay during the grace period ends benefit entitlement, necessitating reinstatement later. Reinstatement requires repayment of past-due premiums plus interest set by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period ends benefits, but reinstatement remains possible within five years provided the applicant proves insurability to the insurer’s satisfaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period ends benefits, but the policyholder retains a five-year window to reinstate coverage by fulfilling required conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period ends benefits, but reinstatement remains possible if overdue premiums and interest are paid, allowing restoration of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that no benefits are payable if the premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, reinforcing the outcome described in fact_sentence_2—that the policy lapses under those conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid before the grace period ends, the policy lapses and no benefits are payable—even if the insured dies afterward. Therefore, the timing of premium payment determines eligibility for the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums within the grace period ensures ongoing eligibility for benefits, which only become accessible once valid proof of death is submitted. Thus, compliance with the payment condition enables the subsequent step of claiming through documented death verification.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="83dd3edd-773f-4f29-83e9-23a815a5a4fe" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is responsible for timely premium payment</data>
</edge>
