</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years provides a pathway to restore benefits even after failure to pay premiums. This complements the incontestability rule by ensuring policies remain viable beyond initial lapses, reinforcing long-term reliability.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
