<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying all past-due premiums, which becomes necessary only if a premium was missed beyond the grace period, resulting in loss of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables recovery</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">Paying all past-due premiums is a necessary step toward reinstating a lapsed policy, thereby qualifying for the exceptions outlined in the Reinstatement provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">Paying all past-due premiums is a necessary requirement for reinstating a lapsed policy within the allowed five-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that unpaid premiums must be settled to restore coverage, which supports the process described in fact_sentence_1 by fulfilling monetary duties required alongside proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">The obligation to pay past due premiums is a foundational step required prior to reinstatement; once fulfilled, the insurer may impose interest charges on those amounts according to its discretion.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains the financial precondition for reinstatement—payment of past due premiums—which enables the temporal provision stated in fact_sentence_2 regarding reinstatement within five years.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the financial requirement for reinstatement—payment of overdue premiums—while fact_sentence_2 specifies the additional underwriting criterion: demonstrating insurability. These elements together define the complete reinstatement process.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the general requirement to pay past due premiums for policy reinstatement; fact_sentence_2 refines this by specifying that interest must also be included in those payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">elaborates on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed premium payments beyond the grace period, it can still be restored provided all outstanding premiums are paid, as outlined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy allows it to remain active again, thereby enabling eligibility for the death benefit should the insured pass away while the policy is in force once more.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables coverage</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
