<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement involving interest on past-due premiums necessitates a written agreement, aligning with the policy's mandate that no changes are valid without written documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">subject to written approval</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement procedures, including the imposition of interest on unpaid premiums, depend on prior written authorization from an official company representative.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on authorization</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Requiring interest on past-due premiums reflects a financial condition imposed by the insurer during reinstatement, consistent with the broader rule that only official representatives may authorize such actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Requiring interest on past-due premiums reflects a standard condition enforced under the policy’s unwaivable terms, consistent with the rule that no agent may bypass established provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder misses a premium payment beyond the 31-day grace period, they may still reinstate the policy only after paying accrued interest, making the grace period a prerequisite for avoiding such charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying accrued interest on overdue premiums, which only becomes relevant once the grace period expires and the policy is no longer automatically in force.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on past-due premiums during reinstatement implies that the policy was previously allowed to lapse due to failure to meet payment deadlines within the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on past-due premiums during reinstatement applies only after the policy has terminated due to failure to pay within the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on delinquent premiums arises specifically because the policyholder failed to meet the deadline during the grace period, resulting in loss of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">Paying interest on past-due premiums enables reinstatement, thereby allowing beneficiaries to retain benefits even after a lapse, consistent with exceptions to termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">Payment of interest on past-due premiums is a prerequisite that must be satisfied when seeking to reinstate a lapsed policy within the allowed five-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">Paying interest on past-due premiums is required when reinstating a lapsed policy, alongside providing acceptable evidence of insurability to satisfy underwriting standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">While interest on past due premiums is not mandatory until reinstatement occurs, it becomes applicable only after the primary condition—payment of outstanding premiums—is met.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on past-due premiums complements the need to provide evidence of insurability, as both are necessary steps to reinstate a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 elaborates on the financial condition required for reinstatement—interest on past due premiums—as part of the process described in fact_sentence_2, which establishes the timeframe for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that interest on past-due premiums is assessed by the company at reinstatement, which directly supports the condition stated in fact_sentence_2 requiring payment of those premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on past-due premiums applies specifically after a policy lapses due to missed payments beyond the grace period, making it dependent on the event described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying overdue premiums with interest, ensuring the policy remains active so the death benefit can be claimed upon the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
