<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years depends on fulfilling financial requirements, including repayment of overdue premiums along with accrued interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional requirement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years depends on proving insurability to the company’s standards. Without meeting this requirement, reinstatement cannot occur despite the time window being available.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years requires payment of overdue premiums plus interest, which is assessed at the moment of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires meeting conditions like paying overdue premiums; since premiums are payable in advance, failure to do so leads to lapse, making reinstitution dependent on prior adherence to payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires payment of overdue premiums, including interest; one option for making such payments is through annual installments.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy allows the continuation of scheduled premium payments, ensuring ongoing coverage through adherence to the originally chosen payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement within five years is conditional upon the policy having previously lapsed due to non-payment beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years provides an exception to standard coverage termination, allowing continuation of benefits upon meeting requirements like paying overdue premiums and proving insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy allows restoration of coverage after it has terminated without value, showing that lapse ends benefits but not necessarily eligibility for revival under certain conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">recoverable after</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy relies on timely payment of overdue premiums and proof of insurability. An Automatic Premium Loan facilitates this process by automatically paying those premiums when due, reducing the risk of permanent lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy enables continued coverage, thereby making the death benefit potentially payable upon the insured’s death, assuming all requirements are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement of a lapsed policy within five years may require the submission of additional documentation to verify eligibility and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after lapse requires meeting certain criteria, including providing any documentation the insurance company deems necessary under its policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years involves paying overdue premiums along with interest; thus, the requirement for interest supports the feasibility of reinstatement under the stated terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement options within five years provide a safety net against lapses caused by missed payments, reinforcing the importance of maintaining steady premium payments—especially when those payments are fixed over the guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years depends on paying back premiums and proving insurability, but the absence of premium increases during the original term makes it easier for the policyholder to afford reinstatement costs, preserving access to affordable coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances stability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years hinges on not having exceeded the grace period; thus, the grace period directly enables the reinstatement process outlined in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms that policies can be reinstated up to five years after lapse, providing operational validation for the time frame mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that reinstatement is permitted within five years of lapse, which depends on timely action after the grace period ends; this implies that the grace period serves as a preliminary buffer before formal lapse occurs, aligning with the continued validity mentioned in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy enables the continuation of coverage necessary for the Death Benefit to be triggered upon the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement within five years depends on meeting policy terms, including those governing the Death Benefit, making the existence and conditions of the benefit relevant to reinstatement viability.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="ad1cb066-961b-4cae-bf88-48a316e04583">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years of lapse depends on paying overdue premiums and proving insurability, making regular payment methods like monthly bank drafts essential for maintaining eligibility to restore coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances reliability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">Although the policy guarantees coverage for 20 years, its reinstatement clause allows revival up to five years after lapse, providing flexibility despite the fixed term limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">supplements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes a universal rule allowing reinstatement within five years after lapse, which supports and contextualizes the specific case described in fact_sentence_1 about the same time limit applying to Jordan Everett Hughes’ policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="8553795c-a210-458d-bbd9-47de9966423a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy enables the fulfillment of the insurer’s commitment to pay the death benefit, making the original guarantee actionable again after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="3c328b68-a332-4773-9c29-f646235f7d51">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement options provide a mechanism through which the policyholder can maintain coverage and satisfy the conditions necessary for receiving the death benefit, aligning with the stipulations outlined in the initial policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement within five years depends on surviving the initial grace period; without it, there would be no opportunity to reinstate since the policy would have already lapsed beyond recovery.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years depends on timely action after a lapse, but only becomes relevant once the grace period expires and the policy lapses, meaning it relies on the prior existence of the grace period provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on grace period</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years enables renewal of coverage, making it relevant when assessing whether the deceased was still covered during the grace period, thus affecting claims processing and deductions like those described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">related to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years provides a remedy for lapses resulting from missed premium payments during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables recovery</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years assumes that the policy was terminated due to nonpayment—a situation explicitly governed by the rule that coverage ends without timely premium payment during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy relies on timely action post-lapse; however, if the grace period expires without payment, benefits cease until reinstatement occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables recovery</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The second statement provides concrete timing (five years) for reinstatement, which contextualizes and validates the exception described in the first statement regarding termination of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">supportees</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 affirms the core principle stated in fact_sentence_1—that reinstatement is allowed within five years—but omits the qualifying requirements detailed in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">supplements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes a five-year window for reinstatement, providing temporal context that makes the requirement in fact_sentence_1 actionable and time-bound.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes the time limit for reinstatement, providing contextual scope for fact_sentence_1’s assertion that unpaid premiums must be settled to restore coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
