<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Payment of past-due premiums with interest is a mandatory requirement enabling the reinstatement of a policy that has lapsed within the allowable five-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that unpaid premiums with interest must be settled to reinstate the policy. This financial requirement follows from the initial necessity of demonstrating insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy necessitates paying overdue premiums along with interest, where the interest rate or calculation method is decided by the insurer upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying overdue premiums with interest; the exact amounts depend on the premium terms detailed in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
