<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement involves paying overdue premiums with interest, which depends on having a clear understanding of available payment modes like monthly billing.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The necessity to pay overdue premiums with interest upon reinstatement arises because premiums are required to be paid in advance; failure to do so leads to lapses, necessitating repayment when restoring coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a policy involves paying overdue premiums with interest, after which future premiums become due on standard due dates aligned with the original payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement requires payment of overdue premiums with interest because failing to pay within the grace period causes the policy to lapse, creating the need for restoration through financial compensation.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to non-payment, it loses all value; however, reinstatement remains possible only if overdue premiums and interest are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Payment of overdue premiums with interest allows reinstatement, preventing full termination of coverage. Without meeting this condition, coverage ends permanently.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest upon reinstatement becomes more significant because the policy lacks an automatic premium loan option, increasing reliance on out-of-pocket funds.</data>
