<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement involves paying overdue premiums with interest, which becomes necessary when a policy lapses due to non-payment. Since the policy does not include an automatic premium loan without a rider, policyholders cannot use borrowed funds to avoid lapse, making reinstatement more critical.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
