  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The determination of interest on overdue premiums occurs at the moment of reinstatement, directly influencing the total amount required to restore the policy’s active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of interest on overdue premiums relies on prior knowledge of the scheduled premium amount and payment terms, which are defined in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The obligation to pay premiums in advance sets the stage for potential delinquency, making it relevant to the calculation of interest on overdue amounts at reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums applies regardless of the payment frequency selected, including annual payments. Thus, choosing annual billing increases the potential amount owed if not paid on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of interest on unpaid premiums occurs when a lapsed policy is reinstated, setting up conditions under which subsequent payments become due again according to the original schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to pay the premium by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses. This lapse initiates the process requiring reinstatement, after which the insurer determines interest on past-due amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums enables reinstatement, which prevents full coverage termination. Without paying accrued interest, reinstatement cannot occur, reinforcing why coverage typically terminates without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums at reinstatement becomes more significant because the policy lacks an automatic premium loan option, meaning policyholders have fewer alternatives to avoid lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">If premiums remain unpaid beyond the grace period, the policy lapses and coverage terminates without value. However, reinstatement remains possible within five years if overdue amounts—including interest—are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional restore</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The amount of interest charged upon reinstatement relies on whether a policy loan can be used to settle outstanding premiums, which itself depends on having enough accumulated loan value.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for additional documentation supports the administrative process involved when calculating interest upon reinstatement, ensuring accurate verification before applying charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for charging interest on overdue premiums arises because applicable laws mandate it, providing the legal foundation for the insurer’s action when reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">mandated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying overdue premiums with interest, which contrasts with the initial guarantee of level premiums, highlighting a shift from predictable cost to variable financial obligation when coverage fails.</data>
  <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">While the first fact emphasizes no premium increases during the term, the second highlights that failure to maintain timely payments can lead to reinstatement fees including interest, thus indirectly reinforcing the importance of consistent payment under the guaranteed terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a missed premium depends on surviving the grace period, during which interest begins accruing on overdue amounts once the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after lapse depends on timely payment of overdue premiums and accumulated interest, making the grace period critical for avoiding the need for reinstatement altogether.</data>
  <data key="d4">necessitated by grace period</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement within 5 years allows for payment of overdue premiums with interest, making the timeline critical for triggering the interest calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy involves paying interest on overdue premiums, enabling continued eligibility for the Death Benefit as outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0b7f99de-0307-43aa-92a2-343af9bb8d66" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines interest on</data>
</edge>
<edge source="31c7ee67-6efa-4d3c-9866-de05b9d546b7" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has past due interest determined by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="207d5b64-5f9e-4ace-ba55-69fb98748e1d" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines interest on past due premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="954296eb-a177-4e72-8e8b-81dac8e89666">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
