  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="96511c59-e7aa-4b77-90a5-4b61ce42dbf5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="a7cf8660-bc76-457d-a656-701faa190468">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">document</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment frequency, which directly informs how much must be paid to reinstate a policy after lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">While the Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment mode, the actual financial consequence of failing to meet those payments—including accrued interest upon reinstatement—is governed separately by the insurer’s policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment options; one such option is quarterly payments, which is explicitly stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment options; one such option is monthly payments, which is explicitly stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits contains detailed premium terms, including allowable payment frequencies like semi-annual billing, making it the source where such options are documented.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment frequency, which directly informs the timing and structure of payments. Since premiums are payable in advance, knowing the payment mode from the schedule ensures timely compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment options, including the ability to pay annually. Therefore, the option to pay premiums annually is explicitly included in the documented terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The payment mode selected by the Policy Owner is reflected in the Schedule of Benefits, ensuring alignment between choices and official records.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The premium amount and payment mode are documented in the Schedule of Benefits, which establishes the basis for determining when future premiums are due under the selected payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The premium amount and payment mode are initially outlined in the Schedule of Benefits, providing the basis for the insurer’s subsequent approval of the chosen mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the current premium mode; altering it requires submitting written notice to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits specifies the current premium amount and mode, which may be altered only after obtaining formal approval from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium terms, including the payment frequency, which determines when the initial payment becomes due. Thus, the first premium’s due date relies on the scheduled payment mode defined earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits specifies the current premium payment mode, enabling the Policy Owner to understand existing terms before requesting a change in frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits specifies the current premium amount and payment frequency, providing essential context for any potential changes requested by the Policy Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The payment terms outlined in the Schedule of Benefits help determine when premiums must be paid, directly influencing whether they are missed beyond the grace period, leading to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The payment terms outlined in the Schedule of Benefits determine whether premiums are met timely, which affects whether the policy remains active. If premiums aren't paid per the schedule, the policy may lapse, resulting in termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the premium amount and payment mode from the Schedule of Benefits ensures timely payments, maintaining the policy in force so that the death benefit becomes payable upon the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ef6ad179-0716-412b-b227-10baa8bdff2f" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">related to premium details</data>
</edge>
