<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments provide a method for fulfilling the financial obligation required to reinstate a lapsed policy within the allowed timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments increase the risk of accumulating significant unpaid amounts over time, potentially leading to higher interest charges upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Since the Schedule of Benefits lists the available payment modes, the possibility of paying premiums annually is derived from and confirmed by that document.</data>
  <data key="d4">implied by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums annually aligns with the overarching rule that premiums must be paid in advance, demonstrating how a specific method fits into the general framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">implied by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates annual payment is permitted, and fact sentence 1 confirms monthly payment is also accepted. These represent alternative choices within the same set of payment frequency options.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative modes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates annual payments are permitted; this complements sentence 1 by providing another valid frequency option among those listed in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates annual payments are accepted; this aligns with fact sentence 1’s mention of semi-annual payments, illustrating different but compatible payment schedules offered under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative mode</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually depends on the Policy Owner’s decision regarding the payment mode. Without the owner’s election, the annual option would not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually relies on the insurance company approving the selected payment mode. Without formal approval, the annual payment method cannot be implemented despite being listed as a possibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments are permitted under the policy terms, and the first such payment is required on the Effective Date, establishing the initial obligation tied to the chosen payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually establishes a payment frequency that determines when future premiums are due. Subsequent premiums align with the periodicity defined by the chosen mode, including annual cycles.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums annually depends on obtaining prior approval from the insurance company before the new payment mode takes effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires approval</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payment is one of the available payment frequencies allowed under the policy terms. The policy owner can initiate changes to adjust how often they pay premiums, including choosing annual payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums annually is one of the options available when changing the payment method. The ability to switch methods allows the policyholder to choose annual payments among other intervals.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments help sustain active coverage; failing to make them timely causes the policy to lapse, resulting in termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The availability of annual premium payments sets the context for when a change in payment mode might occur, necessitating written notice to implement such a shift.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are paid annually but not maintained, it could lead to coverage termination after the grace period expires, unless reinstated per the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments increase the likelihood of cash-flow gaps; if unpaid, they could trigger a need for a policy loan—but only if sufficient loan value exists and the rider is in place.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments help maintain active policy status, which is required for the insurer to disburse the death benefit upon verified claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">precondition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums annually ensures ongoing policy coverage, which is prerequisite for triggering the requirement to submit proof of death when claiming benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">precondition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payment maintains policy continuity, ensuring the insured remains covered so the death benefit becomes applicable upon death. Without current coverage, the death benefit would not be payable regardless of payment method.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
