</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The Company’s approval of the payment mode relies on the details previously specified in the Schedule of Benefits, ensuring alignment with the agreed terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">approves</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode allows for the enforcement of the rule that premiums must be paid in advance according to the agreed-upon schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The company's approval of the premium payment mode allows the policyholder to select options like monthly payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode allows the policyholder to select options like quarterly payments, ensuring compliance with the agreed-upon schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode enables the feasibility of paying premiums on a semi-annual basis, making it a permissible option under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode enables the policyholder to legally use the annual payment option, making it actionable under the terms of the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">After the Policy Owner chooses a payment mode, the Company confirms acceptance of that choice through formal approval, ensuring alignment with policy requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Once the insurance company approves the selected premium payment mode, future installments become enforceable on predetermined due dates aligned with that mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The approved premium payment mode sets the framework for scheduling payments, including determining that the first installment is due on the policy’s effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The insurer’s approval of a premium payment mode follows from a formal request submitted by the policy owner seeking to modify how payments are made.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the initial payment mode sets the stage for future adjustments. The policy owner can later seek modifications to the payment frequency, subject to the insurer’s review and consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of a premium payment mode sets the stage for any future modifications, making it necessary to formally notify them when altering the mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Approval by the Company is required before any change in premium payment mode can take effect. Without formal approval, changes remain inactive.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The approved payment mode sets the due date timeline; failure to meet those deadlines—even after the grace period—results in policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode ensures continuous coverage, preventing premature termination. Without timely payments, even with approved modes, coverage may lapse and terminate without value unless reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode sets the terms under which coverage remains active. If those terms are not met through timely payments, the policy lapses, resulting in loss of coverage and no cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables lapsing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode ensures continuous policy status, enabling eligibility for the death benefit when claimed after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode ensures the policy remains financially viable over time, enabling continued coverage necessary for the eventual triggering of the death benefit claim. Without proper payment arrangements, the policy could lapse before death occurs, preventing any payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">preconditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">After approving the chosen premium payment mode, the insurer may require additional documentation to verify the selection’s validity or ensure compliance with underwriting standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3fa90973-a661-4fcf-8f55-00e515c371f8" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">approves</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f93c77-5ac1-4606-b760-302c2f0f4174" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">approved payment mode</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3235a360-6eb7-4873-9265-640af7bab28f" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">approved payment mode</data>
</edge>
