  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="16ea7d81-660b-4d31-af38-80a43b1e4bb2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">document</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">A request to alter the premium payment frequency depends on knowing the currently scheduled payment mode, which is detailed in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The availability of changing payment frequency depends on the underlying requirement that premiums be paid in advance, ensuring consistency across payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows changes to the frequency of premium payments, enabling the policyowner to select monthly payments among available options.</data>
  <data key="d4">implied by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The ability to request a change in payment frequency allows the policyowner to select from various modes including quarterly payments, thereby enabling them to align their premium schedule with their financial planning needs.</data>
  <data key="d4">example of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The ability to adjust payment frequency includes choosing semi-annual billing as a viable option.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The ability to request a change in payment frequency allows the policy owner to select annual billing, making it feasible to pay premiums once per year.</data>
  <data key="d4">is enabled by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">A request to alter the payment frequency presupposes that a prior payment mode was already elected by the Policy Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">precondition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">A request to alter the payment frequency depends on the company’s willingness to approve it. Without formal approval, any proposed change cannot take effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 grants the policyowner authority to modify the frequency of premium payments. This change directly impacts the timing described in fact_sentence_1, determining when subsequent premiums become due.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The ability to adjust premium payment frequency depends on submitting official written notification to the insurance company, ensuring proper documentation and authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires notice</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to propose altering the premium payment frequency, but the requested change only becomes binding after receiving official approval from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments involves adjusting how often payments occur, which may influence the preferred method used. Conversely, selecting a different payment method might require aligning with available frequencies.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency may help prevent lapse, thereby indirectly helping maintain coverage. However, once a policy has already lapsed, changing payment terms cannot restore its value.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapsing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency may prompt the insurer to request further documentation to verify eligibility or update records.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="198ab335-c096-4f36-b808-396d9cc6b79c" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requests change in frequency of</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e86c9cdb-3aaa-462f-9117-82b5c94c148c" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has changed frequency due to request by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8eddd560-de93-4b49-9149-433aa1a9b50d" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines effective timing of change</data>
</edge>
