  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses—a direct result of failing to meet the payment obligations established in the prior statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to pay within the grace period, the policy lapses regardless of previously selected payment frequency, meaning that even a changed payment method cannot prevent lapse once deadlines pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">preceded by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses, even if a prior request to switch modes was submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, leading to immediate termination of coverage with no residual value.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">If the premium isn't paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses, resulting in immediate loss of coverage with no cash value, unless reinstated per the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">If the premium isn't paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses. However, if an Automatic Premium Loan is activated, the system covers the missed payment automatically, avoiding lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid by the grace period's end, the policy lapses. Since the base policy doesn’t include an automatic premium loan, the policyholder has fewer options to avoid lapse without additional cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid within the grace period, the policy lapses, meaning it is no longer active. As a result, the insurer would not be obligated to pay the death benefit when the insured dies, since the policy was inactive.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses, meaning it ceases to provide benefits including the death benefit. Therefore, the death benefit becomes unavailable unless the policy is reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to failure to pay within the grace period, it ceases to provide benefits, including the death benefit. However, if the insured dies while the policy remains active, the death benefit becomes payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to missed payments, it may no longer provide benefits, including the death benefit. Therefore, timely premium payments ensure that the death benefit remains available.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse occurs when the premium remains unpaid beyond the 31-day grace period, which underscores the importance and function of that grace period established earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">The second fact describes what happens when the grace period expires—policy lapse—which directly follows from the first fact’s assertion that the policy remains in force only until the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapses when the premium isn’t paid by the end of the grace period, but if death occurs earlier during the grace period, the insurer still pays the death benefit less any unpaid premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 summarizes the effect of missing a premium payment beyond the grace period, which aligns precisely with the more detailed timeline provided in fact_sentence_1 regarding when the lapse occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
