<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">When coverage terminates without value upon lapse, the policyholder still retains the option to reinstate it within five years, provided requirements like payment of overdue amounts and proof of insurability are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">precondition for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">A policy’s termination without value creates the scenario where reinstatement becomes necessary, requiring proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage without value after lapse creates the need to repay overdue premiums with interest to restore the policy’s status.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage upon lapse creates the need for reinstatement procedures, including paying overdue premiums along with interest determined by the company at the time of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, it ends without any cash value, meaning that prior knowledge of the required premium amounts and modes—as detailed in the Schedule of Benefits—is essential to avoid such outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The risk of losing coverage without value arises because premiums must be paid in advance; failure to do so leads to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments—even those made monthly—it loses all value, meaning the option to pay premiums regularly becomes irrelevant once coverage has terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value upon policy lapse, it implies that missed payments—even those scheduled quarterly—are sufficient triggers for loss of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments—even those scheduled semi-annually—the coverage ceases entirely and has no residual value.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value upon lapse, it implies that maintaining regular premium payments—including annual ones—is essential to prevent such outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to failure to pay premiums within the grace period, coverage terminates without value. The initial decision to select a particular payment mode impacts the timing and frequency of those required payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to non-payment beyond the grace period, it implies that prior arrangements like approved payment modes were not followed, rendering them ineffective.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of noncompliance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Termination of coverage without value occurs when the policy lapses, often due to failure to pay the required first premium on the Effective Date.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay subsequent premiums on time ensures continued coverage; failing to do so triggers the end of benefits upon policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments, it loses all value regardless of any prior intent to adjust payment frequency. Thus, even if the owner wanted to change the frequency later, the damage is irreversible after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">consequence of lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value due to lapse, any attempt to change the payment method becomes irrelevant after the policy has already expired.</data>
  <data key="d4">consequence of lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">When coverage terminates without value after a lapse, it indicates that the policyholder failed to meet the payment requirement before the grace period ended.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage without value upon lapse is qualified by the possibility of reinstatement, meaning it doesn't apply universally.</data>
  <data key="d4">excepts by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The absence of an automatic premium loan reduces financial flexibility, increasing the likelihood of policy lapse, which leads to termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">If an Automatic Premium Loan is activated, it prevents policy lapse by paying overdue premiums after the grace period, thereby preserving coverage and avoiding termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments, it terminates without any cash value. The death benefit is only available if the insured dies while the policy remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to non-payment, coverage ends with no cash value. Unpaid premiums might be settled via a policy loan only if sufficient loan balance exists, potentially preventing lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapsing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, coverage ceases without value, meaning the death benefit cannot be claimed. Therefore, the death benefit remains subject to the condition that the policy was active at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, coverage ends without value, making the death benefit unpayable regardless of the insured's death. Thus, the ability to receive the death benefit hinges on maintaining active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, coverage ends with no cash value, but if an alternative payment method is desired after lapse, it must be formally accepted by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, coverage ends without value, meaning no death benefit would be payable. Therefore, the payment of the death benefit in a lump sum only applies if the policy remains active until the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, it ceases to provide benefits, but the insurer may still require documentation proving the insured’s death to process any potential claims related to the lapse event.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, it has no value, meaning any potential claim—including a death benefit—is forfeited. Therefore, the death benefit cannot be paid unless the policy was still active at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
