<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years explains why coverage does not terminate without value in all cases; it serves as a safeguard against permanent loss of coverage after lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The absence of reinstatement eligibility leads to permanent termination without value; however, proving insurability restores the possibility of revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on insurability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">If reinstatement does not occur, coverage terminates without value; however, this outcome can be avoided by fulfilling the reinstatement conditions, including paying overdue premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value, reinstatement becomes necessary; however, reinstatement requires payment of overdue premiums including interest, which is determined at the time of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires interest payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Termination without value typically follows from unpaid premiums, which stems from not paying them in advance as required.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums regularly can result in coverage termination without value, although reinstatement remains possible within five years, even if monthly payments were originally selected.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make quarterly premium payments leads to potential loss of coverage without value, underscoring the importance of consistent quarterly payments to sustain benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Failure to maintain regular semi-annual premium payments may result in coverage termination, underscoring the importance of consistent payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make timely annual payments, including those required under the annual payment option, risks triggering coverage termination unless reinstated within the allowed timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates due to non-payment beyond the grace period, it underscores why selecting a feasible premium payment mode is critical to maintaining continuous protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Termination without value occurs when coverage lapses due to non-payment, but only after the initial approval of a payment mode has enabled the policy’s existence and operation.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make timely payments—including the first premium—can result in coverage termination without value, making prompt payment essential to maintain active status before any potential reinstatement window closes.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid on the designated due dates, the policy may terminate without value, despite ongoing obligations outlined in the payment schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The absence of any payout upon policy lapse—except when reinstated—is directly caused by failing to meet the premium payment deadline within the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility allows coverage to continue despite lapse, thereby preventing termination without value in those cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The absence of an automatic premium loan reduces options for maintaining coverage after a missed payment, potentially leading to termination unless reinstated. This highlights why the reinstatement clause exists as a safety net.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a default automatic premium loan feature means policyholders have fewer options to avoid lapse after missed payments, reinforcing why reinstatement becomes critical when coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The risk of coverage termination without value is mitigated if an automatic premium loan is in effect, as it ensures payment of overdue premiums post-grace period, thereby preventing lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">If premiums remain unpaid beyond the grace period, the policy lapses unless reinstated; however, this lapse can potentially be avoided if there is enough accumulated loan value to cover the delinquent payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapsing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses without reinstatement, the death benefit is not payable because coverage has terminated. However, if the policy remains in force at time of death, the death benefit is triggered upon proper documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses without reinstatement, it terminates without value, meaning no death benefit would be payable. Therefore, maintaining active coverage through timely payments ensures eligibility for the death benefit payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value, the death benefit may not be payable unless the policyholder meets reinstatement requirements. Therefore, the death benefit remains dependent on adherence to policy terms, especially regarding active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to provide proof of death ensures proper validation before any claim settlement, even when coverage has terminated. Without submitting acceptable documentation like a certified death certificate, the insurer cannot disburse the death benefit despite the policy being active at time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to non-payment and isn't reinstated, no death benefit is payable. However, if the insured dies while the policy remains active, the company will pay the death benefit upon receiving proper documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b6da7e8-b838-44ed-8d6a-03169f3ad388" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
</edge>
