  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="c0ad6166-0e53-416b-9823-0d101abb92f7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="7b9688f9-c19a-4141-a9f6-efbce73a2b41">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="d04f2023-cd3c-444e-8a19-0be1195fb643">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">document</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The inability to access an automatic premium loan without adding a rider means policyholders lack a built-in mechanism to cover missed payments. As a result, failure to pay leads directly to lapse, increasing the need to reinstate the policy by paying back premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">While the availability of an automatic premium loan depends on adding a rider, this does not alter the fundamental obligation to pay premiums in advance, which remains mandatory regardless of riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">is dependent on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan requires a rider, highlighting that supplementary protections like this are not included by default. Meanwhile, paying premiums semi-annually is a standard option permitted under the policy’s payment flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The need to add an automatic premium loan through a rider parallels the requirement for written notice when switching premium modes, highlighting that non-standard adjustments to policies demand explicit approval processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires documentation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The lack of an automatic premium loan feature means policyholders cannot use borrowed funds to cover missed premiums. Without this safety net, failing to pay within the grace period increases the likelihood of policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan via rider offers a mechanism to maintain coverage post-lapse, thereby reducing the risk of permanent termination despite failure to pay premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not automatically include an Automatic Premium Loan, its inclusion depends entirely on adding a rider or endorsement, making the requirement explicit.</data>
  <data key="d4">necessitates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The addition of an Automatic Premium Loan via rider enables the system to cover unpaid premiums automatically after the grace period ends, ensuring continued policy validity without immediate lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cover unpaid premiums via a policy loan hinges on whether the Automatic Premium Loan provision has been added via rider. Without this addition, the loan option cannot activate even if loan value exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6ec494c-8075-4209-826c-40d27db06e9a" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">issues</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2cd274bb-5c05-48a7-8298-31414d5caf6c" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requests</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0ad6166-0e53-416b-9823-0d101abb92f7" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">added via endorsement</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d04f2023-cd3c-444e-8a19-0be1195fb643" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">does not include</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="a5cd9cd6-1db9-427a-9324-ca6bb84dca8b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
