<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cover unpaid premiums through a policy loan depends on having sufficient loan value, offering a potential pathway to meet the reinstatement requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">If there is insufficient loan value to cover unpaid premiums, the insurer may still charge interest at reinstatement, but repayment would require alternative funds instead of relying on loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to make a semi-annual premium payment, they might rely on a policy loan—if available—to avoid lapsing, highlighting the interplay between payment frequency and financial safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan depends on accumulated loan value, which influences whether delayed annual premiums can be covered without lapsing the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enabling condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cover unpaid premiums with a policy loan relies on having enough accumulated loan value; however, even if used, failure to maintain payments still leads to lapse and loss of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on loan value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to use a policy loan to cover unpaid premiums depends on having sufficient loan value, which helps avoid coverage termination under the reinstatement provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lacks an automatic premium loan provision, then unpaid premiums cannot be covered automatically; instead, reliance shifts entirely to whether sufficient loan value already exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">A policy loan can only apply to unpaid premiums if the Automatic Premium Loan provision was specifically included through a rider; otherwise, no loan functionality is enabled regardless of available funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">enabled by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient loan value is required before an automatic premium loan can be applied to settle delinquent premiums, making it a prerequisite for the process described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">precondition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">If premiums remain unpaid, a policy loan may cover them only when sufficient loan value exists; however, the eventual death benefit remains contingent upon overall policy compliance, including financial obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder uses a loan to cover unpaid premiums, interest must be charged according to applicable laws. The presence of a loan implies ongoing interest accrual.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3bb15d0e-6775-4c86-aef6-e8a0ec564ccc" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">controls loan value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84223b9d-f21c-40ac-b2f9-9fc8e2874dbc" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">uses policy loan to cover unpaid premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3a8c52e6-0628-43bd-81d3-b193fa895947" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can be covered by policy loan if available</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cef91aa1-a198-4101-b9d6-e449268e8f22" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">covers unpaid premiums when sufficient loan value is available</data>
</edge>
