  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit depends on the policy being active at the time of death. If the policy has lapsed due to missed payments beyond the grace period, the death benefit would not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid only when the insured passes away during active coverage. Coverage does not terminate with value if the policy lapses due to nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only paid if the policy remains active at the time of death; hence, failure to maintain coverage (as outlined in the reinstatement clause) prevents any payout, effectively terminating benefits without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit, once triggered by verified proof of the insured's death during active coverage, is directed toward the person specifically named as the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">recipient of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The designation of a beneficiary determines who receives the death benefit, but the actual disbursement depends on compliance with policy terms, including required documentation and eligibility criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only disbursed after proper documentation confirming the insured's passing has been verified by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The designation of the beneficiary determines who receives the death benefit, which is typically paid in a lump sum unless an alternate arrangement is chosen. This clarifies the default distribution mechanism tied to the named recipient.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is typically paid directly to the beneficiary, but if an alternate method of distribution is desired, it must be formally accepted by the insurance company before being applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payout depends on submitting acceptable proof of death, including a certified death certificate, ensuring claims are verified before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
