</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable under active policy conditions; thus, its availability depends on timely premium payments and avoiding lapse, making the timing of payment critical.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable under active policy conditions; hence, its availability hinges on avoiding lapse. Since lapse leads to termination without value, the existence of the death benefit claim depends on sustaining coverage through timely payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit follow policy terms includes provisions like reinstatement after lapse; thus, failure to reinstate means no death benefit despite claims, aligning with coverage terminating without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid according to policy terms includes stipulations like non-inclusion of certain features (such as automatic premium loans), meaning the absence of such a feature aligns with the general contractual constraints affecting payout eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">implied by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
