  <data key="d3">While the death benefit is intended for the beneficiary, its release is contingent on meeting the policy’s stipulated requirements, ensuring proper verification before payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the Death Benefit follows policy terms includes the provision that it is typically paid as a lump sum unless an alternate settlement method is chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate ensures compliance with the policy’s conditions governing the death benefit payment, making it essential documentation for claiming benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
