<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a lump-sum death benefit depends on the policy remaining active, which requires regular advance premium payments as stated in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a lump-sum death benefit depends on the policy remaining in force, which requires regular premium payments—including those made semi-annually—as outlined in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">A lump-sum death benefit is payable only when the policy is active at the time of death, meaning failure to maintain premium payments could prevent this outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid in a lump sum only if the policy is still active; if it has already lapsed, the policyholder receives nothing, making the existence of a lump-sum payout dependent on avoiding lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">A lump-sum disbursement is standard for the death benefit, but only after proper documentation confirming the insured's death during active policy coverage has been received.</data>
  <data key="d4">payment form</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">The standard payment of the death benefit in a lump sum applies unless a different settlement option is elected; this ensures the beneficiary receives the full amount under normal circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The default lump-sum payout of the Death Benefit is part of the broader contractual conditions governing its disbursement under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains term</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">If a beneficiary chooses an alternative to the standard lump-sum payment, they must obtain prior approval from the insurance company. This ensures compliance with company policies before altering the default death benefit disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires approval</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid in a lump sum unless another option is selected, and this payout requires verified proof of death, including a certified death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid in a lump sum only after proper documentation confirming the insured's death has been accepted by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">precondition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">If an alternative settlement option isn't elected, the death benefit is paid in a lump sum; this payout happens quickly once proper proof of death is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid as a lump sum upon the insured’s death unless another option is selected, establishing the start point for interest accumulation from the date of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is typically paid as a lump sum, subject to any election of an alternate settlement option. The individual entitled to receive this payment is determined by the latest written beneficiary designation filed with the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="ad1cb066-961b-4cae-bf88-48a316e04583">
  <data key="d3">A lump-sum death benefit payout depends on the policy remaining active through timely premium payments, including those made via the designated monthly bank draft system.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">The provision that the death benefit is paid in a lump sum applies specifically to claims made during active coverage, including those occurring within the 20-year guaranteed period established by the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4">
  <data key="d3">A successful reinstatement within 5 years after lapse preserves the right to receive the death benefit as a lump sum, aligning with the default payout method described in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="8553795c-a210-458d-bbd9-47de9966423a">
  <data key="d3">The default lump-sum payment mechanism supports the fulfillment of the insurer’s obligation described in the first statement, ensuring timely delivery of benefits per policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff" target="3c328b68-a332-4773-9c29-f646235f7d51">
  <data key="d3">The standard lump-sum payment of the Death Benefit in fact_sentence_2 aligns with the overarching terms governing benefits mentioned in fact_sentence_1, reinforcing procedural consistency.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
