<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 notes that alternative death benefit settlements require Company approval. Fact sentence 1 indicates that altering the premium payment mode similarly depends on Company consent. Though related in process (approval necessity), they concern separate functional areas of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires approval</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for company approval of alternative settlement options becomes relevant only after a policy has lapsed, meaning the need arises from the termination of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">condition for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for company approval of alternative settlement options implies oversight over how benefits are distributed after death. This complements the first statement by ensuring that even if the death benefit is triggered, its distribution method may need formal consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces restriction</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Company approval is required for any non-standard settlement options, ensuring that even when the death benefit is intended for the beneficiary, its delivery mechanism remains subject to insurer consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Approval by the company for an alternative settlement option implies that such options exist under the policy but are conditional upon meeting defined criteria, thereby reflecting constraints tied to the broader death benefit provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Approval by the company is required before any non-lump-sum settlement option can take effect, thereby directly influencing how the death benefit is distributed per the initial terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The need for an alternative settlement option to be approved by the company depends on having proper documentation confirming the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">If an alternative settlement option is selected, the insurer may require extra documentation to verify eligibility or compliance before approving it.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 requires company approval for alternative settlements, and fact_sentence_2 explains that the company may impose further documentation demands as part of its evaluation process.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Alternative settlement options require company approval, which depends on having a legally recognized beneficiary. The beneficiary’s identity, established through official documentation, determines eligibility for receiving benefits under any settlement method.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
