<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies a standard document type used to fulfill the proof-of-death condition mentioned in fact_sentence_1, enabling payment of the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">enabler</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Providing a certified death certificate enables the timely processing and payment of the death benefit to the designated beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Providing a certified death certificate satisfies a critical term needed to activate the death benefit payment under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is necessary to verify the insured’s passing, enabling the insurer to disburse the death benefit as a lump sum, as stated in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate serves as acceptable proof of death, fulfilling the condition outlined in fact_sentence_1 regarding satisfactory documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate establishes a foundational proof; however, insurers may demand supplementary materials to validate claims fully.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate serves as essential documentation that satisfies the requirement for proving death, enabling the insurer to process the claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes a baseline requirement for proof of death. Fact_sentence_2 expands on this by allowing the insurer to request supplementary documents beyond the minimum standard.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate ensures proper validation before any benefits are processed, enabling accurate calculation and disbursement of the death benefit including accrued interest after the date of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary for any claim, including one made by the designated beneficiary. Without accepted evidence like a certified death certificate, even the rightful beneficiary cannot collect the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death requires a certified death certificate, but only the designated beneficiary may submit it. Without knowing who the beneficiary is, submitting proof would lack proper authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via certified death certificate enables the processing of the death benefit, but only if the policy was actively maintained through timely premium payments during its guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via certified death certificate enables payout upon the insured’s passing; if the policy was previously lapsed due to unpaid premiums, reinstatement may still be possible within five years provided the grace period has not expired.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death, such as a certified death certificate, is necessary to trigger the death benefit, but only applies when the policy was still in force at the time of death—ensuring the grace period’s role in preserving coverage is critical.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate enables the insurer to process a death benefit claim, especially if the policy was previously reinstated within the 5-year timeframe allowed after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death through a certified death certificate is essential to initiate the payment of the Death Benefit under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death, such as a certified death certificate, is necessary to activate the Death Benefit, which is explicitly bound by the policy’s stated terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="ad1cb066-961b-4cae-bf88-48a316e04583">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is essential for claiming the death benefit; without ongoing premium payments like those made through monthly bank drafts, the policy would have lapsed before the claim could be processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death through a certified death certificate enables the payment of benefits only if the policy was still in force at the time of death, which is ensured by the 20-year guaranteed period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61" target="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via certified death certificate supports claiming benefits after death, whereas the five-year reinstatement rule enables revival of a lapsed policy before expiration, representing complementary procedural requirements across distinct phases.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
