<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Receiving the death benefit requires the policyholder to have maintained active coverage through consistent premium payments in advance, making prior compliance essential for benefit entitlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit quickly upon receiving proper documentation depends on the policy being active, which requires regular premium payments—including annual ones—as outlined in the terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">A death benefit is payable only if the policy is active at the time of death. If the policy had already lapsed before death, the benefit would not be available, regardless of subsequent proof being submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">A death benefit is only payable if the policy was active at the time of death; otherwise, it terminates without value, except under reinstatement terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 adds detail about timely processing and the standard of proof (“satisfactory”) when paying the death benefit. Fact_sentence_1 provides the foundational rule that payment follows receipt of due proof, forming the basis for the refinement in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Payment to the beneficiary depends on timely verification of death through accepted evidence like a certified death certificate, ensuring claims are processed correctly.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for timely payment hinges on the existence of defined policy terms governing when and under what conditions the death benefit is issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Prompt payment of the death benefit depends on submitting acceptable proof of death, ensuring the beneficiary receives the lump sum as intended when no other settlement method is chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Upon receiving acceptable proof of death, the company initiates prompt payment of the death benefit, making compliance with documentation requirements essential for timely settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">responds to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Receipt of a certified death certificate allows the insurance company to fulfill its obligation to disburse the death benefit without delay.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The prompt payment of the death benefit depends on the successful submission of satisfactory proof, including any additional documentation requested by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Prompt disbursement of the death benefit depends on providing acceptable proof, which the Company defines through its reasonable documentation requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">Upon receipt of satisfactory proof of death, the insurer disburses the death benefit, triggering the start of interest accrual from the date of death until actual payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid to the designated beneficiary once proof of death is received; therefore, identifying the correct beneficiary is essential for claim processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
