<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary establishes the primary recipient; if they do not survive, the policy’s payout defaults to the policy owner, ensuring continuity in distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">fallbacks to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the identity subject to potential change. This foundational clarity allows the policy owner to legally update the beneficiary via a written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">defines for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes eligibility criteria; if none survive the insured and the owner is deceased, the death benefit defaults to the owner’s estate, extending the beneficiary rule to its legal fallback.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional outcome</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the subject of potential changes; therefore, it provides essential context for understanding when those changes become legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the basis for whom the policy owner can designate or modify through formal submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">defines for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the basis for eligibility, enabling the enforcement of automatic生效 of beneficiary changes even if the insured has passed away.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the subject of any potential change; therefore, it provides essential context for understanding how and when a change becomes effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the legal basis for changing designations. Since changes take effect upon receipt regardless of the insured's condition, the initial identification of the beneficiary is essential for determining the scope of such modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary establishes eligibility, but their actual rights are contingent upon whether an assignment has been made, meaning the beneficiary’s authority may be restricted under such circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary relies on formal designations made through proper channels, which are initiated by the policy owner’s authorized actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the beneficiary, as defined in the first sentence, establishes the recipient eligible for the death benefit payment described in the second sentence. This foundational definition supports the policy owner’s right to determine payout terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
