<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes become effective at signing, independent of future events like the insured’s survival. This contrasts with the first sentence, which applies only when no survivorship occurs, making it a contingency rather than an action-triggered event.</data>
  <data key="d4">timing dependence</data>
