<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to change the beneficiary relies on having a clear understanding of who the current beneficiary is, as defined in the initial statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner can change the beneficiary at any time while the insured is alive. This authority ensures that the intended recipient aligns with current wishes, particularly relevant in cases where the original beneficiary does not survive the insured—making it possible for the policy owner to receive the benefit under such circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that beneficiary changes are allowed during the insured’s lifetime, providing contextual limitation. Fact_sentence_1 affirms the broader authority to make such changes via written request, encompassing the scenario described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change the beneficiary at any time during the insured’s lifetime provides the basis for the rule that such changes become effective once signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a written request allows the beneficiary change to become effective upon receipt by the company, regardless of the insured’s current health or survival status.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request, and this action triggers immediate生效 (effectiveness) once signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request, and this action automatically becomes effective once received by the insurer, even if the insured has passed away before or after submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's ability to change the beneficiary is contingent on whether an assignment has been made; such assignments impose limitations on the owner's rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary is a specific manifestation of the broader right to request beneficiary designations, illustrating how the policy owner exercises control over beneficiary assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary is one specific action within the range of rights held by the policy owner, who also possesses the general power to request additional riders such as an Accelerated Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request; in turn, the company commits to responding promptly by supplying necessary information.</data>
  <data key="d4">responds to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary requires a written request from the policy owner, establishing who receives benefits; once designated, the policy owner can then select how those benefits are distributed.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the policy owner to change the beneficiary relies on being legally recognized as the owner, which occurs automatically if no name is provided, per fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by an authorized officer ensures that beneficiary changes—like those permitted in fact_sentence_2—are formally documented and legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">While the policy allows owners to initiate beneficiary changes freely, these actions still require submission through official channels per the restriction that no unauthorized agent or broker may alter the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">While the first statement restricts waiver of policy provisions, the second allows beneficiary changes through proper documentation, demonstrating that such modifications fall under permitted administrative processes rather than provision waivers.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
