<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The timing rule for beneficiary changes relies on knowing who currently holds the role, making the initial definition foundational to applying the effectiveness condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect at signing, ensuring timely implementation. This contrasts with the default case described in the first sentence where no beneficiary survives, highlighting how proactive changes prevent estate distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The moment a beneficiary change is signed determines its effectiveness, relying on the prior right granted to the policy owner to make such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">This sentence repeats the prior statement verbatim, reinforcing that the change takes effect on the date of signing, maintaining internal coherence within the chunk.</data>
  <data key="d4">reiterates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 identifies the signing of the request as the triggering event for a beneficiary change. This aligns with fact sentence 1, which confirms the change takes effect even if the insured has passed away, validating the significance of the signature date over survival status.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The moment a beneficiary change is signed determines its effectiveness, relying on the prior authorization granted to the policy owner to make such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">preceded by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The change of beneficiary takes effect from the signing date, and this rule applies even if the insured has passed away before the company receives the request.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">A beneficiary change becomes effective upon signing, but if the policy has been assigned, those rights may be restricted by the terms of the assignment agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">A beneficiary change requires prior authorization from the policy owner, who holds the legal right to make such requests. Without this right, the change could not occur at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect upon signature, enabling the policy owner to control who receives benefits; this decision supports the subsequent choice of how those benefits are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="90ec6e29-a29c-4e3c-8d1b-c21dc571dc89">
  <data key="d3">The rule that beneficiary changes take effect upon signature allows for potential modification of Elaine M. Hughes’ role as primary beneficiary, meaning her entitlement is conditional on no subsequent change being made.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables change</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="d13623e0-a45f-4060-82e1-dbdfcb46c827">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of changing beneficiaries—such as naming Morgan L. Hughes as contingent—is governed by the requirement that the change be signed, making the process described in fact_sentence_2 essential to establishing the beneficiary hierarchy mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec">
  <data key="d3">Any alteration to the beneficiary designation must comply with the written-and-signed requirement set forth in the original contract terms, ensuring legal enforceability despite immediate生效 upon signature.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change upon signing (fact_sentence_2) depends on the policy owner having the legal authority to make such changes, which is affirmed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries upon signing reinforces the policy owner’s autonomy, aligning with their explicit right to assign the policy and exercise full ownership privileges.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries underscores the policy owner’s autonomy, which includes the related right to cancel the policy at any time during the initial review period.</data>
  <data key="d4">complementary rights</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The immediate effectiveness of beneficiary changes underscores the importance of the owner’s examination right, ensuring accurate and timely modifications based on understanding.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs decision</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="83582c0a-3af4-481f-98d3-0102afbf3328" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
