  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="29a2056c-8360-4a9b-a22d-9fd6ab9090d6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">rider</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes are binding once received, even if the insured has passed away; thus, knowing who the current beneficiary is (defined in sentence 1) determines the legitimacy and impact of any update.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes take effect at the time of receipt by the company, independent of the insured’s life status, thereby influencing the outcome specified in case no beneficiary survives—the updated beneficiary or the policy owner may receive the death benefit accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The immediate effectiveness of a beneficiary change—regardless of the insured’s survival—depends on the policy owner having submitted a formal written request, highlighting the primacy of the owner’s action in triggering the update.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">Regardless of the insured’s survival status when received, the beneficiary change remains effective as of the signing date, ensuring continuity of intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Each sentence independently confirms that beneficiary changes take effect upon receipt by the company, irrespective of the insured’s survival, creating a redundant but consistent statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">identical</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">Regardless of the insured's survival status, a submitted request to change the beneficiary takes immediate effect upon receipt by the company, ensuring the policy owner's intent is honored without delay.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">Regardless of the insured’s survival status when received, the beneficiary change remains effective as of the signing date, ensuring continuity of intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how beneficiary changes become effective immediately upon receipt, independent of the insured's status. This autonomy supports the policy owner’s authority discussed in fact_sentence_2 regarding assignments, reinforcing overall control over policy disposition.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes take immediate effect upon submission by the policy owner, even if the insured has passed away. This reflects the power vested in the policy owner to make such decisions unilaterally.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="90ec6e29-a29c-4e3c-8d1b-c21dc571dc89">
  <data key="d3">The rule allowing immediate effectiveness of beneficiary changes applies directly to the case where Elaine M. Hughes was named primary beneficiary, meaning her status could be modified without regard to the insured’s living condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="d13623e0-a45f-4060-82e1-dbdfcb46c827">
  <data key="d3">The rule allowing immediate effectiveness of beneficiary changes applies directly to the scenario where Morgan L. Hughes is named contingent beneficiary, enabling the policyowner to modify or remove her eligibility at any time before the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">While a beneficiary change takes immediate effect regardless of the insured’s condition, the availability of an Accelerated Death Benefit Rider adds significance to ensuring correct beneficiary designation, particularly if the insured expects to claim benefits before death.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that beneficiary changes are effective immediately upon receipt, reinforcing the importance of proper documentation under fact_sentence_1; without adherence to the written-signed rule, no change—even one received—would be enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">complies with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The rule that beneficiary changes take effect upon receipt, even if the insured is no longer alive, depends on the policy owner having the legal authority to make such changes, which is confirmed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries independently of the insured’s survival supports the policy owner’s autonomy, reinforcing their capacity to assign the policy, as both actions reflect core ownership privileges outlined in the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries without requiring the insured’s survival complements the owner’s right to cancel, both illustrating the extent of unilateral decision-making authority granted to the Policy Owner under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change the beneficiary without requiring the Insured’s survival supports the Owner’s autonomy, reinforcing why having an examination period is essential to ensure deliberate use of such powers.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e592c9c5-3a37-4935-8ba3-03155cf57086" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">does not affect effectiveness of change</data>
</edge>
