  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71" target="dbcf3642-dbfc-4205-bbd3-b724a2b9a2d8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">rider</data>
</edge>
<edge source="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">While the policy owner can legally assign the policy, they assume full accountability for potential tax consequences arising from the assignment, which the company explicitly avoids.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits right to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">While fact sentence 2 focuses on tax consequences arising from an assignment, it logically follows from the broader principle established in fact sentence 1—that the company does not validate or guarantee the legality of such actions. Both statements serve to limit corporate liability.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The absence of corporate liability for tax consequences underscores why the rights tied to the policy must conform to the conditions set forth in any assignment agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffee15b2-60a8-4087-81ba-317dd5b4c4fd" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has no tax responsibility for assignment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e984cb9-338f-4bfd-bb39-623d7f23e18a" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">may lead to assignment with tax consequences</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f03646b-653f-41ec-b4c2-bf1536c757f3" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">subject to tax consequences upon assignment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb243f5c-cc42-4378-8f12-e15be38bb37f" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can result in tax implications when used post assignment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dbcf3642-dbfc-4205-bbd3-b724a2b9a2d8" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">associated with possible tax burden upon acceleration and assignment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="a3d633b9-8cd1-4eb0-9263-0ab53acef03f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="3e78f375-e698-4ded-b4ba-188dbd376334">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="da2383d9-f942-47d2-b12c-4bf32df2a640">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="95ab5b61-4eee-4a88-9e6b-9f98ab325360">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="6be2618a-11dd-4dae-8416-0b04af47fbcc">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="2d09a4fe-6b90-429a-854f-92e9362ba4bd">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">document</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="dcf922ce-2307-41b7-9f1d-680e60397d50">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="09ee9dcf-5a4a-446f-bce7-9a5cd245a8e1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="afa5d7c3-d841-4d90-8762-5c5554fec8b4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">rider</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">If an assignment exists, it overrides or limits the beneficiary’s rights; thus, the beneficiary’s role is dependent on prior administrative actions involving ownership transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The rights of the policy owner and beneficiary are constrained by the terms of any assignment, meaning even if the owner would normally inherit the death benefit, an assignment might prevent this outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The rights of both the policy owner and beneficiary are limited by the existence of a policy assignment. In cases where the owner dies without a survivor, the assigned terms might determine whether the estate inherits the death benefit instead.</data>
  <data key="d4">affects outcome</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt by the policy owner to change beneficiaries may be restricted or governed by prior assignments, making the ownership right subordinate to assigned contractual conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The rights of the owner and beneficiary are constrained by assignment terms, meaning even a properly signed beneficiary change might not override binding assignment conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">Assignment agreements restrict the policy owner’s authority to modify beneficiaries, thereby limiting the practical exercise of the right described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The rights of the owner and beneficiary are constrained by assignment terms, meaning even a properly signed beneficiary change might not override binding assignment conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy owner can legally assign the policy, the resulting transfer limits the scope of rights available to both the owner and the beneficiary under the new arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">The rights of the owner and beneficiary are limited by the terms of the assignment, which implies that the company cannot ensure such assignments' legal standing or enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">implied by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">Assignment terms govern the rights of the owner and beneficiary, making it necessary to consider potential tax impacts even if the company does not assume responsibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The ownership right to obtain a policy copy may be restricted if the policy has been assigned, as assignments can limit certain owner privileges.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">The right of the owner and beneficiary may be limited by an assignment, but if the policy is canceled, those rights cease altogether since no further benefits are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">terminates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to determine the death benefit payout method is contingent upon not being restricted by prior assignments, which govern the distribution of benefits under certain conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">The right of the policy owner and beneficiary may be restricted by prior assignments, which could affect how settlement choices are exercised. This constraint indirectly influences the implementation of any elected settlement method.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3e78f375-e698-4ded-b4ba-188dbd376334" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">bound by assignment terms</data>
</edge>
<edge source="95ab5b61-4eee-4a88-9e6b-9f98ab325360" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">bound by assignment terms</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="49a8ef1e-73d4-47ca-b71a-8b70a5af08c8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="776cca52-932d-49a6-ad07-7b2e8691fcdb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="853dd85c-7f1a-4b04-8937-9f4889ec0c6e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="37b99e89-7ad8-49e1-bb5a-cb10a92ac37a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="4f405853-d5f2-4d71-939e-23223681fcd2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="56ef4f4f-ebd6-40c8-8883-2b50d2331092">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">document</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="7b3dbbdd-e274-467e-8bca-07eed3653cc9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="f8ade05b-c761-4355-9a8f-38bb6521439d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="c0bf0b97-e1e1-431a-9e78-8b6ab0059b61">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">rider</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to end the policy through a written request, resulting in the immediate cessation of insurance coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to terminate coverage anytime through a formal request, resulting in the cessation of all future benefit payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">When the policy owner cancels the policy, it initiates a process that results in refunds of unearned premiums according to applicable laws.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cancel the policy reflects broad control over its existence, enabling the owner to terminate coverage whenever desired. This autonomy supports the broader capacity to manage beneficiary designations, ensuring alignment with current intentions.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states the policy owner’s power to terminate coverage unilaterally. This autonomy supports the broader capacity described in fact_sentence_2, where the owner can seek supplemental provisions such as riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cancel the policy underscores the Policy Owner’s ultimate control, which includes modifying beneficiaries, ensuring alignment with the owner’s autonomy over the policy’s structure and benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cancel the policy underscores the owner’s authority over its lifecycle, making the power to assign it more meaningful, as assignments require active ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Fact Sentence 2 specifies the mechanism and timing for cancellation—submitting a written request anytime—which directly supports and operationalizes the broader right described in Fact Sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">expands upon</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The power to cancel the policy anytime reinforces the significance of the initial examination right, allowing the Owner to review terms thoroughly before deciding to retain or terminate coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37b99e89-7ad8-49e1-bb5a-cb10a92ac37a" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has cancellation right</data>
</edge>
<edge source="56ef4f4f-ebd6-40c8-8883-2b50d2331092" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is required for</data>
</edge>
<edge source="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd" target="e338bc4a-f84d-4f61-ad7e-225750db7762">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd" target="4286b80f-c1e7-4215-8844-a6c306032ae6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd" target="d364744e-065e-4368-b6dc-f86174f38d21">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
