<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to request beneficiary designations provides the mechanism through which individuals become officially recognized as beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">source of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to request beneficiary designations allows them to influence who receives the death benefit, thereby potentially preventing the need for payment to themselves under the contingency specified in the other statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to designate beneficiaries directly affects the conditions under which the death benefit may go to the estate instead of an individual beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The right to request beneficiary designations encompasses the specific action of changing them via a formal submission, making it foundational to the process described in the other statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">encompasses</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to designate beneficiaries directly supports the mechanism by which a change takes effect upon signature, making it actionable.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner possesses the legal right to designate or modify beneficiaries, which directly supports the implementation of changes that take effect independently of the insured’s life status.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to designate beneficiaries directly supports the mechanism by which a change takes effect upon signature, making it actionable.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner possesses the legal right to designate or modify beneficiaries, which directly supports the implementation of changes that take effect independently of the insured’s life status.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The right to request beneficiary designations encompasses the ability to change beneficiaries, showing that the former includes the latter as a concrete application.</data>
  <data key="d4">includes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Requesting beneficiary designations establishes the intended recipient(s) of proceeds, which informs decisions about whether and how to assign the policy, ensuring alignment with the owner’s wishes regarding asset distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs assignment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">The right to designate beneficiaries allows the owner to determine who receives benefits after death. This authority complements the option to cancel the policy, reinforcing overall ownership control over the policy’s lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Requesting beneficiary designations requires knowledge of policy details, which the Policy Owner can obtain by requesting a copy of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 highlights the Policy Owner’s authority to view beneficiary designations, whereas fact sentence 1 refers to retrieving past premium payment records. These are independent yet complementary rights concerning policy transparency.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's right to request beneficiary designations triggers the insurer's responsibility to provide the necessary information in a timely manner.</data>
  <data key="d4">responds to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 highlights the Policy Owner’s authority over beneficiary assignments, while fact sentence 2 extends this autonomy to include selecting supplementary benefits such as riders. Together, they reflect the breadth of decision-making power vested in the Policy Owner regarding policy customization.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner exercises their right to request beneficiary designations, prompting the company to comply by providing the necessary information according to law.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The right to designate beneficiaries allows the Policy Owner to determine who receives benefits; this foundational choice directly informs subsequent decisions about how those benefits are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights the specific capability to request beneficiary changes, reinforcing the foundational right stated in fact_sentence_1. Without this actionable power, the right would lack practical application.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to designate beneficiaries complements the right to assign the policy, since assigning it often involves transferring future benefit distribution decisions to a new owner who can update those designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to designate beneficiaries supports the overall autonomy of the policy owner, which includes the separate right to terminate the policy at any time during its term.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The owner’s power to request beneficiary designations relies on having access to the policy through the examination right, enabling proper management of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
