  <data key="d4">document</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="c4c59cc0-e959-4aec-9e93-b7e03f1112a2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="73f40b38-bbb9-44ed-995f-9c5441912af4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="3213f233-8bb0-4769-958f-7da716bae2b2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">rider</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The right to request riders includes potential modifications like adding benefits tied to beneficiary designations, but changing a beneficiary itself does not require a rider and operates independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights the policy owner’s authority to obtain additional features like riders. This right complements the flexibility implied in fact_sentence_1, where the owner can end the policy entirely if desired.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 enhances the scope of information available to the policy owner beyond just the main policy, reinforcing the right established in fact_sentence_1 by ensuring full transparency about attached provisions such as riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 addresses the Policy Owner’s entitlement to know about additional policy features such as riders, which complements fact sentence 1 by expanding the scope of accessible policy information beyond just premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 addresses the Policy Owner’s ability to add riders, which may influence how beneficiaries receive proceeds; thus, it indirectly supports the context of beneficiary management described in fact sentence 1, though not directly dependent on it.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may initiate requests for additional riders or endorsements, and the insurance company commits to providing the necessary information in a timely manner after receiving such a request.</data>
  <data key="d4">responds to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may initiate a request for additional riders or endorsements, and the company is obligated to fulfill this request by providing the necessary documentation in compliance with law.</data>
  <data key="d4">responds to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to request riders includes potential access to benefits like an Accelerated Death Benefit, which directly relates to how the death benefit is settled—supporting flexibility in choosing payment methods.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to request riders includes potential access to features affecting settlement options, making it relevant to changes in those options. However, actual implementation depends on predefined terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders enhances the functionality of beneficiary designation, allowing the owner to customize payout conditions beyond standard arrangements, thus supporting more flexible beneficiary management.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders allows the owner to customize the policy, potentially influencing future assignment decisions by altering benefits or conditions associated with the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders expands the policy’s functionality, which may influence decisions about cancellation; however, the right to cancel remains intact regardless of rider inclusion, ensuring ultimate flexibility for the owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The owner’s ability to request riders depends on having prior access to the policy content; thus, the examination right facilitates meaningful engagement with supplemental options offered under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="91d25b60-f533-46da-9fe8-b15e0ba87488" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has right to request riders or endorsements</data>
</edge>
