  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s power to choose the settlement method implies control over disbursement terms, which becomes relevant only after determining who qualifies to receive the benefit—such as under the rule stated in the first sentence regarding the policy owner being the recipient if no beneficiary survives.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Selecting the method of death benefit payment depends on having an established beneficiary; thus, prior beneficiary designation allows for informed choices about settlement options.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">Selecting or modifying the death benefit payment method depends on having active authority over beneficiary designations, such as changing them after signing, ensuring alignment with current intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">Selecting or modifying the death benefit payment method depends on having active authority over beneficiary designations, such as changing them after signing, ensuring alignment with current intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">Selecting the method of death benefit payment depends on having already identified a beneficiary, making it contingent on prior beneficiary designation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The existence of an assignment limits the scope of the policy owner’s rights, potentially restricting their ability to unilaterally alter how the death benefit is distributed to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Selecting the method for paying the death benefit requires knowledge of policy terms, making access to a policy copy essential for exercising this right effectively.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Choosing the method of death benefit payout depends on prior beneficiary designation, making it contingent on having established who the intended recipient(s) are.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Choosing how the death benefit is paid influences whether certain riders, such as those enabling early payouts, might be relevant, thus informing decisions about requesting specific endorsements.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to choose or alter the death benefit payment method, but this decision cannot be implemented without prior approval from the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
