  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">exclusion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="44890f02-1230-4458-a32b-7eb7306db82a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">right</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="afb3fa96-3d41-443e-8c78-a37a3b80db6c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">legal notice</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider serves as a particular illustration supporting the more general claim that policies offer optional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is described as an optional add-on; it enables partial pre-death payouts from the death benefit when certain conditions are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is an optional add-on that permits early access to policy funds when certain conditions are met, such as a terminal illness diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider enables early access to policy funds upon qualifying conditions. One such requirement is a confirmed terminal illness with a prognosis of 12 months or less.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is an optional add-on feature offered within the policy. Its maximum payout is capped at 50% of the policy’s face amount, defining its financial limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is an optional provision enabling early access to policy benefits under specific conditions. To qualify, a licensed physician must certify the policyholder's life expectancy, ensuring clinical validation of eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is offered as an optional add-on; however, any payments made through it are limited by a cap established by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider depends on fulfilling specific requirements, including submitting medically verified documentation to substantiate the diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is an optional provision within the policy that enables early access to benefits under specific conditions. To utilize this rider, the policyholder must initiate the process by submitting a formal written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">The presence of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider enables the possibility of early benefits, which triggers the need for rigorous medical validation processes such as obtaining a second opinion.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is an optional add-on that enables early access to part of the policy’s death benefit under specific conditions. When activated, the payment directly reduces the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is offered as an option; interest accrued on any advance from this rider reduces the remaining death benefit payable upon the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">The presence of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider enables early access to policy funds under certain conditions. When benefits are paid out, any existing loans are subtracted from the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider enables early payouts upon terminal diagnosis, but excludes cases where the illness was intentionally self-inflicted, ensuring protection against abuse.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">The presence of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider enables early payouts under certain conditions, and one factor affecting the final payout amount is the deduction of any existing liens from the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider enables early payouts upon terminal diagnosis, but excludes payments if the illness arises from war-related causes, ensuring coverage does not apply in such cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider provides early access to policy funds upon diagnosis of a terminal illness, but payment is denied if the illness resulted from criminal activity like a felony.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider provides a mechanism for early payout under specific conditions. The policyholder retains control over this process by being able to cancel their request before funds are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is an optional add-on that enables early access to policy funds upon diagnosis of a terminal illness. Revocation of a payment request requires formal written notification to the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">exists within</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider as an optional feature, which explains why it appears in the policy details mentioned in fact_sentence_1, confirming its inclusion was intentional and part of standard offering terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider depends on the Death Benefit defined in the policy; without it, the rider would have no basis for payment distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s governing terms explicitly define what benefits are allowed and under what circumstances; therefore, any additional benefit like the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider must conform to these established rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The written amendment rule reinforces the legitimacy of adding or utilizing riders such as the Accelerated Death Benefit, which cannot take effect without formal documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Any inclusion or use of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider necessitates adherence to the policy’s formal amendment process requiring signature by an authorized officer.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Policy modifications like adding the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider must follow the restriction stated in fact_sentence_1, meaning no unauthorized party can initiate such changes, preserving control over contractual alterations.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The policy provision prohibiting unauthorized waivers supports the controlled implementation of riders like the Accelerated Death Benefit, ensuring such enhancements follow required legal and administrative protocols.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
