<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">Eligibility for the accelerated death benefit hinges on the rider being available through the policy, making it contingent upon the inclusion of optional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis triggers eligibility for the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which is only applicable if the rider was previously added to the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">Being diagnosed with a terminal illness directly enables the possibility of receiving an early payment from the death benefit under the rider's terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Having been diagnosed with a terminal illness is a required step that enables consideration for the accelerated benefit, but only if accompanied by a short life expectancy.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">A diagnosis of terminal illness triggers eligibility for the accelerated benefit, but confirmation of limited life expectancy requires formal certification by a licensed physician to validate the claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires certification</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis makes an individual eligible for the accelerated benefit, but without submitting a formal written request, no payment can occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">A diagnosis of a terminal illness makes an individual eligible for the accelerated benefit, but the actual payout is constrained by a cap set at 50% of the policy's face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis makes an individual eligible for the accelerated benefit, but only if they provide medical documentation approved by the company to support their claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires documentation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">If an individual is diagnosed with a terminal illness, they may qualify for the accelerated benefit; however, the actual amount paid cannot exceed the maximum limit established by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis enables access to the accelerated benefit under the rider. Upon approval, the received funds directly lower the remaining death benefit payable at the time of the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">If an individual is diagnosed with a terminal illness, they become eligible for the accelerated benefit; however, the company may require a second medical opinion to validate the diagnosis before approving payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional verification</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">Once an insured person meets the qualifying condition of a terminal illness diagnosis, they become eligible for the accelerated benefit, triggering subsequent reductions in the death benefit due to administrative charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">Qualifying for the accelerated benefit due to a terminal illness initiates the payment process, during which existing policy loans are subtracted from the available benefits to determine the net payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">If an individual is diagnosed with a terminal illness, they may qualify for the benefit; however, this qualification does not apply if the illness was caused by war-related activities.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">If an individual is diagnosed with a terminal illness, they may qualify for the accelerated benefit, but only if the illness was not intentionally self-inflicted.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">If an insured person meets the diagnostic criteria for a terminal illness, they become eligible to access part of their policy's face value. Interest accrues on this advance and reduces the eventual death benefit paid out upon passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">If an individual is diagnosed with a terminal illness, they may qualify for the accelerated benefit; however, this eligibility is nullified if the illness was caused by participating in a felony.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">If an insured person meets the criteria for a terminal illness, they may access accelerated benefits, leading to adjustments in the death benefit where existing liens are subtracted from the remaining payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">A person must first qualify by being diagnosed with a terminal illness to even initiate a request for accelerated benefits. This condition enables the subsequent possibility of withdrawing that request before payment occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">If an individual meets the criteria for a terminal illness, they may initiate a claim for accelerated benefits. They retain the option to revoke their request at any time before payout by submitting written notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">A qualifying diagnosis for benefits does not inherently depend on honesty about past disclosures; however, concealing information could invalidate the claim regardless of eligibility status.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the qualifying event—a terminal illness—that triggers the use of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider already noted in fact_sentence_1, making it applicable under defined circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">enabled by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis triggers access to part of the Death Benefit, but only within the constraints set forth by the policy’s governing terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a conditional benefit available under the policy, which directly falls under the scope of "benefits" referenced in fact_sentence_1, making it contingent upon adherence to the stated terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">subsumed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 introduces a specific exception allowing early payouts, it operates independently of the broader rule requiring written consent for policy changes, though compliance with such rules may apply during claim initiation.</data>
  <data key="d4">complies with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Eligibility for the accelerated benefit may trigger a policy amendment involving disbursement, which would need to comply with the rule that changes require authorization from an approved company officer.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers process</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the accelerated benefit provision implies that certain policy changes are allowed under strict conditions, even though no agents or brokers may otherwise modify the policy without authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables exception</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The accelerated benefit provision relies on documented, authorized processes, aligning with the broader policy restriction that only official representatives may authorize changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">complies with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
