<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">A required life expectancy of 12 months or less defines one of the criteria for qualifying for an accelerated death benefit rider, which is among the optional riders available on the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">A life expectancy of 12 months or less qualifies individuals for accelerated benefits under certain riders. This specific threshold applies to the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which is one optional add-on offered on policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less qualifies the policyholder to trigger the early payment feature under the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">A life expectancy of 12 months or less is a mandatory condition that applies specifically to individuals already diagnosed with a terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the life expectancy criterion for accessing benefits, while fact_sentence_2 ensures this criterion is formally verified through documentation from a qualified healthcare provider.</data>
  <data key="d4">validated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis with a life expectancy of 12 months or less qualifies the policyholder for accelerated benefits, subject to the cap of 50% of the policy's face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a 12-month life expectancy determines initial eligibility, while the maximum payment limit controls how much can be received once eligible. These conditions function separately in determining benefit availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis with a life expectancy of 12 months or less qualifies the policyholder for consideration of benefits, making it necessary to proceed with a formal application via a written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a 12-month life expectancy triggers the need for validation via a second medical opinion to ensure accuracy and prevent misuse of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis with a life expectancy of 12 months or less qualifies the policyholder for an accelerated benefit payment under the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">eligibility condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness diagnosis with a life expectancy of 12 months or less triggers eligibility for benefits, necessitating accompanying medical documentation to verify the claim's validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder meets the diagnostic criteria of having a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less, they become eligible for an accelerated benefit. Administrative charges associated with processing the claim are deducted from the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder meets the terminal illness criteria with ≤12 months life expectancy, they may access accelerated benefits. Subsequently, outstanding loans are subtracted from the remaining death benefit during payout computation.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder qualifies under the 12-month life expectancy rule, they may receive an accelerated benefit whose repayment includes accumulated interest, reducing the eventual death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder meets the 12-month life expectancy criterion due to a terminal illness, they may qualify for benefits unless the illness was intentionally self-inflicted, which disqualifies them despite satisfying the initial condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder meets the diagnostic criteria (terminal illness with ≤12 months life expectancy), they become eligible for an accelerated payment. This payment reduces the final death benefit, and any outstanding liens are subtracted from the adjusted balance at that time.</data>
  <data key="d4">eligibility leads to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the medical threshold for eligibility based on prognosis, while fact_sentence_2 adds a behavioral exception that overrides eligibility regardless of medical status.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder has a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less, they meet a key eligibility requirement. However, even if this condition is met, payment is denied if the illness was caused by war-related activities.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets a medical requirement for qualifying for accelerated benefits, while fact_sentence_2 highlights that falsifying information during the process constitutes fraud, potentially invalidating claims based on such criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a 12-month life expectancy serves as the qualifying condition for accessing the accelerated death benefit provided by the rider mentioned in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">condition for access</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Eligibility for early withdrawal from the Death Benefit due to terminal illness hinges on the policy’s established terms governing the Death Benefit itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables access to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a specific benefit trigger dependent on clinical criteria, which falls within the scope of "benefits" referenced in fact_sentence_1 and thus operates under the policy’s governing terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Access to early payouts due to terminal illness depends on documented approval processes, aligning with the need for written agreements mandated in the main policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Eligibility for early benefit disbursement hinges on documented proof verified through processes consistent with the need for authorized corporate approval outlined in the policy's amendment rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Eligibility for early payouts due to terminal illness depends on formal, authorized actions per policy rules, aligning with the restriction that no unauthorized modifications are permitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces requirement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the medical condition required to qualify for early benefit payouts, but its implementation depends on adherence to proper channels—such as written requests approved by officials—which aligns with the restriction stated in fact_sentence_1 about who may act on behalf of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
