  <data key="d3">A physician's certification of life expectancy is necessary for accessing certain riders, highlighting that such provisions depend on specific policy add-ons being present.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician must verify the policyholder’s life expectancy as part of the process to activate the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, confirming its legitimacy and necessity within the rider’s framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification of life expectancy is required to qualify for the early payment under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">Life expectancy must be certified by a licensed physician, which serves as essential validation that an individual meets the criterion of having 12 months or fewer to live after being diagnosed with a terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">validates condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">The need for a licensed physician's certification (fact_sentence_2) exists specifically to validate whether the patient meets the 12-month life expectancy threshold defined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification of life expectancy confirms eligibility for the rider, enabling consideration of the maximum allowable benefit amount determined by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician must certify the policyholder’s life expectancy to qualify for benefits, ensuring the claim meets the criteria necessary to access the capped payment allowed under the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician must certify the policyholder's life expectancy of 12 months or less before any claim can proceed. This medical validation enables the subsequent submission of a formal written request for benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician must certify the policyholder's life expectancy, and this certification must be supported by medical documentation deemed acceptable by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification of life expectancy provides the initial basis for eligibility, upon which the company may exercise its right to confirm the assessment via an independent medical evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification of life expectancy is required to initiate the accelerated benefit claim, ensuring legitimacy before any financial disbursement occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification of life expectancy is required to initiate the accelerated benefit claim. After approval, any administrative charges are deducted from the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification confirms the policyholder meets the terminal illness criteria necessary to trigger the accelerated benefit process. This eligibility step precedes any financial calculations, including deductions for existing loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification of life expectancy is required to initiate the accelerated benefit claim. After approval, any accrued interest on the paid benefit is deducted from the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification of life expectancy ensures that the terminal illness meets clinical criteria, including ruling out deliberate causes like self-injury, thereby determining eligibility under exclusions such as those specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification confirms the insured's terminal diagnosis and expected survival time, enabling consideration for benefits. However, even with such certification, payments are withheld if the underlying cause was criminal activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician must certify the insured’s life expectancy, ensuring clinical validity; any falsification of such certification constitutes fraud under state law.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician's certification of life expectancy ensures accurate eligibility assessment, preventing false claims that could trigger fraud allegations. This procedural safeguard supports enforcement of anti-fraud policies like those outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents fraud</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician’s certification of life expectancy is required to activate the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, making it a prerequisite for receiving advance payments from the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">While the Death Benefit is generally bound by policy terms, the process for receiving part of it early depends on clinical confirmation of limited life expectancy, reinforcing that even core benefits require adherence to specified procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes a prerequisite (physician certification) needed to claim a benefit, which aligns with fact_sentence_1’s assertion that all benefits are bound by policy rules and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="df9797d7-629e-4917-bc56-582d8cf4fe9d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for physician-certified life expectancy creates a vulnerability that could be exploited in cases of insurance fraud, suggesting that fraudulent acts might circumvent proper medical verification procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Life expectancy certification per fact_sentence_2 relies on proper documentation, reinforcing the broader rule in fact_sentence_1 that no policy-related action is valid without written approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">A licensed physician’s certification of life expectancy serves as critical documentation needed when requesting policy adjustments related to accelerated benefits, thereby requiring adherence to formal authorization protocols established in the main policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">While no direct modification of the policy occurs due to life expectancy certification, the process reinforces the need for official approval pathways outlined in the first statement, maintaining control over claim-related adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">complies with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 reinforces that all policy adjustments—including those linked to riders like the Accelerated Death Benefit—require official approval, supporting the necessity of physician certification as part of legitimate procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
