  <data key="d3">The restriction on benefits being capped at 50% of the face amount applies specifically to the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, one of the optional riders available.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The cap limiting payments to 50% of the face amount applies specifically to the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which is described as an optional rider available to policyholders.</data>
  <data key="d4">sets cap</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The cap limiting payouts to 50% of the face amount ensures that only a defined fraction of the death benefit may be accessed early through the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">While the policyholder may qualify upon being diagnosed with a terminal illness, the benefit received is limited to no more than half the policy’s face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits qualification</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed—up to 50% of the face amount—is only applicable once the policyholder meets the diagnostic requirement of having a life expectancy of 12 months or less.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">The maximum benefit available under the rider is limited to 50% of the policy’s face amount, which applies only after qualifying conditions—including physician-certified life expectancy—are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable benefit is limited to 50% of the face amount only after a formal request has been submitted to initiate the process.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 illustrates a specific instance of the broader rule in fact_sentence_2, showing that the company-imposed maximum limit is concretely defined as 50% of the policy’s face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the maximum allowable benefit at 50% of the face amount, which can only be accessed after submitting required medical proof. Fact_sentence_2 ensures that such claims are substantiated through company-approved documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the maximum allowable benefit, ensuring financial limits are respected; fact_sentence_2 ensures accurate eligibility assessment through independent medical review, supporting compliance with those limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed under the rider is limited to half the policy's face amount, ensuring that any payout has a proportional impact on reducing future benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits amount</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">The 50% cap on payments sets an upper bound for accelerated benefits, while outstanding loans are subtracted from the remaining death benefit after acceleration, affecting the final payout amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable acceleration is capped at 50% of the face amount, and any interest accruing on that advance contributes directly to diminishing the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">The maximum benefit is capped at 50% of the face amount, but this cap does not apply if the illness stems from intentional self-injury, effectively nullifying the benefit in such cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">The 50% cap on accelerated benefits limits the total possible payout, while outstanding liens further reduce the actual amount paid out, ensuring the remaining death benefit reflects pre-existing debts.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable payout is capped at 50% of the policy’s face amount, ensuring that any benefits paid out do not exceed this threshold. Administrative charges further diminish the remaining death benefit, meaning even within the 50% limit, the net payout may be reduced due to additional costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">The maximum benefit is capped at 50% of the policy's face amount, but this limit does not override exclusions such as payments being denied when the illness stems from criminal activity like a felony.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">The presence of the rider allows partial pre-death payouts, which are restricted by the rule that no more than 50% of the face amount may be paid out, ensuring financial constraints align with policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The rule mandating written approval for policy changes supports the enforceability of the 50% cap on accelerated death benefits, confirming that such limitations are formally documented and binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Any change to the maximum allowable payout under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider would require a signed amendment by an authorized company officer, consistent with the policy’s requirement for written approvals.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The 50% cap on the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider illustrates a pre-defined limitation that aligns with broader policy rules requiring written approval for changes, reinforcing compliance with established terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The 50% limit on the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider reflects a pre-defined policy term that aligns with broader restrictions requiring written approval for changes, reinforcing compliance with established provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
