<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">The company's role as the policy issuer justifies its ability to impose a cap on benefits paid through the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">justified by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a maximum limit on payments from the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider implies that not all riders operate without restrictions; thus, it reinforces the idea that some riders come with predefined conditions, supporting the broader claim about optional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">Since the rider has a maximum payout determined by the insurer, the initial mention of its availability naturally leads into constraints governing how much can be received.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The provision allowing early receipt of a portion of the death benefit operates only within the bounds established by the company's maximum allowable payment threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">The maximum amount payable under the rider constrains the potential benefit available to individuals who meet the qualification criteria, such as being diagnosed with a terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">While the 12-month life expectancy threshold sets who qualifies, the payment ceiling ensures that even qualified individuals cannot exceed a predefined dollar amount, regardless of need.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains eligibility</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a company-set maximum benefit influences the scope of what can be paid out, contingent upon proper documentation like a physician-certified life expectancy.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes a general principle—that the payment is capped by the company—which is made precise by fact_sentence_1 specifying that the cap equals 50% of the policy’s face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed under the rider depends on the insurer's approval of qualifying medical documentation submitted with the request.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">The Company's right to require a second medical opinion ensures that claims for accelerated benefits align with established guidelines, including the maximum permissible payout. This oversight helps validate the legitimacy of the claim before any funds are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable payment under the rider determines how much the death benefit will be reduced when benefits are paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable benefit amount is determined by the insurance company, setting a ceiling on potential payouts. This financial constraint applies once the policyholder has initiated the claim process through a formal written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable payment under the rider constrains the total benefit available before any reductions. Administrative charges are deducted from this capped amount when calculating the final death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed under the rider determines the initial principal amount from which interest is calculated, directly influencing how much the death benefit is reduced over time due to accrued interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">The maximum benefit allowed by the company sets an upper bound on payments, but actual disbursement may be reduced due to pre-existing loans that diminish the adjusted death benefit upon acceleration.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed by the company influences the total funds available after adjustments like liens. Outstanding liens reduce the adjusted death benefit, thereby affecting how much of the capped amount remains accessible.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
