  <data key="d3">A written request must be submitted by the policyholder to initiate the accelerated benefit payment process.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">After submitting a written request, the insurer may require a second medical opinion to confirm eligibility for the accelerated benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a written request initiates the process that results in the application of administrative charges, which are deducted from the death benefit when the accelerated benefit is paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">A written request from the policyholder initiates the acceleration process, enabling the insurer to disburse funds subject to conditions including future reductions due to accumulated interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a written request initiates the claim process, leading to evaluation where existing loans are considered in adjusting the remaining death benefit. This ensures accurate accounting once funds are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a written request initiates the claims process, enabling the insurer to assess eligibility and calculate the adjusted death benefit, including deductions for outstanding liens.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">A written request is required to access accelerated benefits, but such payments are voided if the terminal illness stems from criminal activity, including felonies.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional exclusion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a written request initiates the process for receiving accelerated benefits, enabling the policyholder to later withdraw their application before funds are paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">A written request is required to initiate the accelerated benefit process; however, payment will not be made if the illness was intentionally self-inflicted, rendering the request ineffective under such circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional exclusion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">A written request is required to begin receiving the accelerated benefit, establishing the first formal step in the claims process. This requirement enables the subsequent ability to revoke the request via written notice before any funds are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a written request is a prerequisite for receiving benefits, and knowingly falsifying information during this step constitutes insurance fraud, reinforcing the need for truthful submissions.</data>
