  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">exclusion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="fd28798f-201b-4ac6-b2e4-0119c627a713">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">exclusion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="45086005-035e-4569-9298-029fef641dac">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">right</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="d7996b1a-bbae-41f2-a50a-9be9d62924b7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">legal notice</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">The rule excluding payments when the terminal illness results from intentional self-injury applies uniformly across policies issued by Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">covered by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">A restriction on payment due to intentional self-harm applies specifically to the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which is one of the optional riders available under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on payments due to self-inflicted injuries applies specifically to claims made under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, limiting its coverage scope.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">If an illness stems from intentional self-inflicted injury, the eligibility established by the rider does not apply, effectively blocking any early payout despite diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">A diagnosis of terminal illness alone does not guarantee payment; the cause must not involve intentional self-harm to maintain eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Even if a policyholder has a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less, they cannot receive the accelerated benefit if the illness resulted from deliberate self-injury, making the life expectancy criterion insufficient on its own.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness stems from intentional self-infliction, it disqualifies the claim even if a physician certifies a short life expectancy, meaning the certification cannot override this specific exclusionary rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness was intentionally self-inflicted, no acceleration occurs regardless of whether it meets the 50% threshold, making the financial cap irrelevant in that scenario.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Even if a written request is submitted, the beneficiary cannot receive benefits if the terminal illness resulted from deliberate self-injury, making the procedural step irrelevant in those cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">preempts procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness arose from intentional self-infliction, the claim cannot proceed regardless of supporting medical documents, making such evidence insufficient in this case.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes based on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Exclusions for self-inflicted injuries justify the need for a second medical opinion to validate the cause of illness and prevent abuse of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">justified by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness was intentionally self-inflicted, no accelerated benefit is paid, so the death benefit remains unchanged due to lack of payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 excludes benefits for illnesses resulting from self-harm, while fact sentence 2 extends this principle to include crimes. Together, they form part of a broader set of exclusions aimed at preventing abuse of the benefit system through intentional harm.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 excludes payments when the terminal illness stems from self-harm; similarly, fact_sentence_2 excludes payments when it arises from war-related activities. Both statements function as independent disqualifying conditions tied to intent or external conflict.</data>
  <data key="d4">exclusionary parallel</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness stems from self-harm, no benefit is payable. Concealing such details intentionally would violate anti-fraud provisions, potentially invalidating claims even beyond the self-harm clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness stems from self-inflicted harm, no accelerated benefit is paid. This aligns with broader prohibitions against fraud, such as knowingly providing false information to obtain benefits unlawfully.</data>
  <data key="d4">related to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">While the rider permits accelerated benefits for qualifying terminal illnesses, its application is explicitly barred if the condition arises from intentional self-injury, thus creating a clear exception to the general provision outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to rider</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The rule that no accelerated benefit is paid due to self-inflicted injury qualifies the general application of the Death Benefit, reinforcing its dependence on specific conditions set forth in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 illustrates a specific limitation on benefits due to intentional harm, which falls under the overarching condition described in fact_sentence_1 that all benefits are bound by policy terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a specific exception to benefits that complements fact_sentence_1's requirement for written validation, reinforcing that even special payouts must adhere to defined, documented rules to prevent abuse.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a limitation on accelerated benefits due to self-inflicted harm, which would fall under the category of exceptional circumstances requiring review—a process consistent with the requirement in fact_sentence_1 that such decisions need official validation.</data>
  <data key="d4">suppressed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of benefits for intentionally self-inflicted injuries supports the principle that only authorized actions lead to policy outcomes, reinforcing the rule that agents cannot unilaterally override terms set forth in the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces restriction</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 restricts accelerated benefits in cases of self-harm, reinforcing the principle in fact_sentence_1 that unauthorized actions cannot override policy rules; thus, such exclusions are upheld via proper administrative control.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="baef86a8-1a7f-4323-ac53-f71a639c1e15" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">subject to exclusion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4fde93d8-3db9-423c-99b6-f47f80782f76" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eeeff1f4-408e-4af9-bcec-241ec61bcef7" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">excluded if</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1834dccd-7992-4e5c-8838-54b82671ea29" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">excluded if</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ead7487d-e4ee-41c9-a779-5babe3dd7697" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">causes exclusion of accelerated benefit</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="45dc6ecc-80a4-4473-89d1-403fadf61614">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
