  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes submitting false information as fraud, which aligns with the broader principle in fact_sentence_2 that intentionally concealing material facts also qualifies as fraudulent conduct.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines fraud broadly as filing applications or claims with materially false information. Fact_sentence_2 builds on this by specifying that such acts become legally recognized fraudulent insurance behaviors when done intentionally to deceive.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that providing false information on claims is fraud. Fact_sentence_2 explains that such acts require intentional deception about material facts, refining the legal standard for accountability.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="df9797d7-629e-4917-bc56-582d8cf4fe9d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 provides the legal standard defining insurance fraud, which directly applies to the event described in fact_sentence_2—a confirmed fraudulent insurance act.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="9e3cd4f3-d236-4040-a6c4-c46f3a22a611">
  <data key="d3">The legal principle defining material falsehoods in insurance applications applies directly to cases like Eleanor B. Raynor's, whose authoritative role may involve overseeing claims processes vulnerable to fraudulent manipulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
